 standards – safe and gentle for both mums and babies.\n\nTested and Loved by Real Mums\n\nOver 1,000 mums have tested and trusted our products for unbeatable comfort and performance.\n\nDriven by Innovation\n\nOur patented DoubleFit™ design delivers a better, more comfortable breastfeeding and pumping experience.\n\nMobile Style™\n\nPump The Way You Like\n\nGood experience\n\n\"This was an absolute breeze to use. I think it's really worth the price, it's amazing quality, really well made and comes with everything needed to make it a good experience. I found this really effective and it doesn't fall around once in my bra. It's smooth, doesn't feel too heavy, and really is discreet.\"\n\nAmy\n\nFAQs\n\nIs It Good to Use Electric Breast Pumps?\n\nYes. Electric breast pumps are a great choice for breastfeeding mums looking for convenience and efficiency. They can help maintain or increase milk supply, especially for working mothers or those with low supply issues. Choosing the right electric breast pump means finding one that offers strong suction power, quiet operation, and easy-to-use features. A comfortable and effective electric breast pump can make your breastfeeding journey smoother and more successful.\n\nHow Many Minutes Should I Use an Electric Breast Pump?\n\nFor most mums, starting with 15–20 minutes per pumping session is recommended, gradually adjusting based on your milk supply and comfort. Everyone's needs are different, so listen to your body and pump according to what feels best for you.\n\nFactors like your milk production, your baby’s feeding schedule, and your comfort all play a role. Stop pumping if you feel any discomfort or when your breasts feel empty to avoid over-pumping, which can cause soreness or irritation. Using your electric breast pump correctly helps maintain a healthy milk supply and a comfortable breastfeeding experience.\n\nDo Wearable Pumps Decrease Milk Supply?\n\nA wearable pump does not decrease milk supply, as long as it provides strong and effective suction. Suction strength is key to fully emptying the breast, which helps maintain a healthy milk supply.\n\nWearable pumps like the Momcozy S12 Pro are designed with high suction power to ensure efficient milk removal, so you can pump hands-free without compromising your milk production.\n\nWhich Is Less Painful: Manual or Electric Breast Pump?\n\nPain during pumping varies from mum to mum, but many breastfeeding mothers find electric breast pumps to be less painful because they offer multiple adjustable suction levels and modes, allowing you to customise comfort and reduce nipple pain. However, using too high suction, especially with sensitive nipples or elastic nipples, can still cause discomfort.\n\nSome mums prefer manual breast pumps because they provide more control over suction and pumping speed, which can help minimise pain. Yet, manual pumps may cause hand and wrist fatigue when used for long sessions.\n\nRegardless of whether you choose a manual or electric breast pump, selecting the right breast pump flange size and adjusting the suction level correctly are essential for reducing pain, preventing nipple soreness, and ensuring a comfortable pumping experience.\n\nHow Do I Choose an Electric Breast Pump?\n\nChoosing the right electric breast pump can make all the difference for busy mums. Here are key factors to consider:\n\nPortability:\nIf you pump on the go or at work, choose a lightweight, portable breast pump like the Momcozy M6 that fits your lifestyle.\n\nSuction Power:\nLook for a pump with strong and adjustable suction to effectively express milk and maintain a healthy milk supply.\n\nComfort:\nThe right fit matters, so try different pumps and flanges to find one that feels comfortable and prevents nipple pain or discomfort.\n\nFeatures:\nConsider useful features such as double pumping for efficiency, quiet operation for discretion, rechargeable batteries for convenience, and app control for personalised pumping sessions.\n\nPicking the right electric breast pump tailored to your needs helps make breastfeeding easier, more comfortable, and more efficient.\n\nHow should I clean and sterilize M6 accessories?\n\nWash M6 accessories with regular dish soap. If sterilisation is needed, boil them for 5 minutes, then air dry, wipe dry, or use low-temperature drying. Do not use microwave sterilisation. For steam sterilising, drying, or hot-air drying, keep the temperature within 100°C / 212°F when possible and do not exceed 110°C / 230°F. M6 accessories can also be cleaned in a Momcozy bottle washer, but please do not use Storage mode. Avoid alcohol-based cleaners, as they may affect the soft silicone on the flange.\n\nWhy does the suction feel weaker after cleaning or sterilizing?\n\nSuction may feel weaker if the milk collector or flange is slightly deformed after excessive heat exposure, which can affect the airtight seal. Please check whether the accessories are fully dry, properly installed, and free from warping, gaps, or damage. To help maintain strong suction, avoid microwave sterilisation and keep steam sterilising, drying, or hot-air drying within the recommended temperature range.\n\nHow customers say about\n\n4.8\n\nRated 4.8 out of 5 stars\n\nBased on 627 reviews\n\n5\n\nRated out of 5 stars\n\n525\n\n4\n\nRated out of 5 stars\n\n89\n\n3\n\nRated out of 5 stars\n\n9\n\n2\n\nRated out of 5 stars\n\n1\n\n1\n\nRated out of 5 stars\n\n3\n\n98%\n\nwould recommend this product\n\nSlide 1 selected\n\nReviews\n627\n\n(tab expanded)\n\nQuestions\n\n(tab collapsed)\n\nFilters\n\nWrite a Review\n(Opens in a new window)\n\n627 reviews\n\nSort\n\nMost Recent\n\nOldest\n\nMost Helpful\n\nPhotos & Videos\n\nHighest Rating\n\nLowest Rating\n\nLeast Helpful\n\nJM\n\nJada M.\n\nVerified Buyer\n\nReviewing\n\nMomcozy Mobile Style™ Hands-free Slim Breast Pump | M6\n\nI recommend this product\n\nRated 5 out of 5 stars\n\n1 week ago\n\nYes.\n\nI've used it twice. The first time i had some leakage but 