\n\nSize Guide\n\nFAQ\n\nShipping & Delivery\n\nReturn & Exchange\n\nCommunity Discount\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nContact Us\n\nHome\n\nBreastfeeding\n\nMomcozy Air 1 vs M5 Smart (2026): Which Wearable Fits\n\nWritten by\nMomcozy Care Team\n\nUpdated on\nAugust 28, 2026\n\nMomcozy Air 1 Ultra-slim Breast Pump\n\n$314.99\n\n$369.99\n\nAdd to Cart\n\nShop Now\n\nSpecial Offers For You\n\nChoosing between the Momcozy Air 1 vs M5 breast pumps can significantly impact your breastfeeding journey. Both wearable breast pumps offer hands-free convenience, but they cater to different needs and budgets. The Momcozy M5 vs Air 1 debate centers on one key distinction: smart technology versus traditional simplicity.\n\nThe Momcozy Air 1 comes with smart app control, which allows you to pair it with your mobile device to customize your pump sessions, monitor your activity, and use professional modes. On the other hand, M5 comes with simple manual operation and an LED display. All these features will be discussed in this all-encompassing guide. Let’s dive deeper and see which one is suited for you.\n\nUpdate\n\nBest-seller M5 is now\nM5 Smart\n!\n\nConnect to the\nMomcozy App\nto track volume and control sessions from your phone.\n\n✓ Smart Tracking\n\n✓ App Control\n\nShop Now\n\nAir 1 vs M5 Smart at a glance\n\nSpec\n\nAir 1\n\nM5 Smart\n\nThickness / weight\n\n61 mm / 260 g\n\n74 mm / 230 g\n\nSuction (max)\n\n280 mmHg, 15 expression levels\n\n285 mmHg, 9 levels\n\nCup\n\n180 ml, transparent top\n\n160 ml\n\nBattery\n\nWireless case ~15 sessions\n\n~6 sessions, Type-C on the cup\n\nApp\n\nSensor: auto mode, full-cup alert\n\nRemote levels, milk log, reminders\n\nDouble price\n\n$369.99\n\n$199.99\n\nAir 1 is not the quiet headline. If silence is the whole brief, that’s\n\nM9\n, not this table. M5 Smart is still in the catalog. It is not the new M-series host after the next Ultra lands. Don’t treat this page as a Willow teardown. Willow Go is a real slim rival with its own app and bags. If you’re already in that system, stay. If you want our case plus a sensor ping when the cup is full, Air 1 is the comparison that matters.\n\nSmart Technology and Control Options\n\nWhen comparing\n\nthe Air 1\n\nand\n\nM5\n\n, the biggest difference lies in how you control them. The Air 1 is fully app-driven, while the M5 uses traditional onboard controls. Here’s a breakdown of each experience.\n\n4.7\n\nRated 4.7 out of 5 stars\n\n140\n\nMomcozy Air 1 Ultra-slim Breast Pump\n\n$314.99\n\n$369.99\n\nAdd to Cart\n\nShop Now\n\nMomcozy Air 1 App Control Features\n\nThe Air 1's standout feature is its smart app connectivity, transforming your smartphone into a complete pumping control center.\n\nSetup and Connection\n\nGetting started is straightforward: download the Momcozy app, create an account, and connect your pump via Bluetooth by pressing the pump's power button for 3 seconds and tapping \"Add Device\" in the app.\n\nRemote Control and Monitoring\n\nThrough the Momcozy app, you can adjust all settings remotely. You can enable bilateral control to operate both pumps at once or switch between them individually. The app allows you to select modes (Auto, Manual, etc.), adjust suction levels, and view milk volume in real-time, even providing a \"Full milk alert\" when full.\n\nAdvanced Pumping Modes\n\nThis data-driven approach helps you optimize pumping schedules. Beyond basic controls, the app unlocks exclusive professional pumping patterns:\n\nMilk Boost™ enhances milk production through scientifically optimized pumping rhythms\n\nMilk Relief™ gently eases engorgement discomfort while effectively expressing milk\n\nMyFlow™ Mode allows complete customization of stimulation, expression, or mixed modes.\n\nTracking and History\n\nWhen finished, the app auto-records your session (or you can adjust it manually). You can then view your complete pump history by Day, Week, or Month in the \"Records\" tab.\n\nMomcozy M5 Manual Controls\n\nThe M5 features a full LED screen that displays pumping modes, intensity levels, and session duration directly on the device. All adjustments are made using physical buttons on the pump, providing tactile feedback and at-a-glance monitoring without requiring your phone. This traditional approach appeals to mothers who prefer simplicity or want to minimize screen time.\n\nUpdate\n\nBest-seller M5 is now\nM5 Smart\n!\n\nConnect to the\nMomcozy App\nto track volume and control sessions from your phone.\n\n✓ Smart Tracking\n\n✓ App Control\n\nShop Now\n\nThe Air 1 uses a minimalist indicator light system instead of a screen, relying entirely on the app for detailed information and control.\n\nPumping Performance and Power\n\nAvailable Pumping Modes\n\nMomcozy Air 1 and M5 have these three basic modes for expressing that simulate nursing:\n\nStimulation Mode is typically characterized by fast-paced sucking rhythms for stimulating a\nletdown reflex\n\nExpression Mode features slower and deeper suction to facilitate efficient milk expression\n\nMixed Mode involves faster stimulation followed by prolonged expression phases\n\nSuction Strength Comparison\n\nThe Air 1 offers much stronger suction performance with 15 levels of suction compared to 9 levels on the M5.\n\nFeature\n\nAir 1\n\nM5\n\nMaximum Vacuum Strength\n\nUp to -280 mmHg\n\nUp to -240 mmHg\n\nStimulation Mode\n\n-67.5 to -172.5 mmHg\n\n-52 to -113 mmHg\n\nExpression Mode\n\n-105 to -280 mmHg\n\n-105 to -240 mmHg\n\nMixed Mode\n\n-67.5 to -280 mmHg\n\n-52 to -240 mmHg\n\nCycle Speed Performance\n\nHere is a breakdown of the cycle speed ranges (cycles per minute) for each mode:\n\nFeature\n\nAir 1\n\nM5\n\nStimulation Mode\n\n54-90 cycles/min\n\n50-120 cycles/min\n\nExpression Mode\n\n25-60 cycles/min\n\n23-57 cycles/min\n\nMixed Mode\n\n46-84 cycles/min\n\n6-16 cycles/min\n\nThe Air 1 has a greatly improved maximum vacuum power, which is especially useful for mothers with\nclogged ducts\n, low milk supply, or for those for whom more vacuum is required for efficient milk expression.\n\nDesign and Physical Features\n\nOverall Design Philosophy\n\nThe Momcozy Air 1\nfeatures a distinctive tear-drop shape (125mm × 110mm × 61mm) with a sleek, streamlined appearance available in one color. Its unique flat base provides excellent stability when placed on surfaces, preventing spills during pumping or milk transfer.\n\nThe Momcozy M5\nfeatures a semi-circular design (128mm × 117mm × 74mm) with 4 color options. The round base makes it slightly more delicate to maneuver when not in use but ensures it is space-efficient.\n\nComponent Count and Assembly\n\nAir 1 Components\n(6 main parts):\n\nMotor, flange, diaphragm, valve, milk collector, milk collector back cover\n\nUSB Type-C cable, magnetic charging cable, flange cover\n\nM5 Components\n(5 parts):\n\nMotor, flange, diaphragm, valve, milk collector\n\nUSB Type-C cable, flange cover\n\nThe M5's simpler design means faster assembly and disassembly—particularly helpful during exhausting early morning or\nlate-night pumping\nsessions.\n\nFlange Design and Sizing\n\nThe Air 1 utilizes soft, flexible flanges that conform gently to the breast, potentially enhancing comfort during extended pumping sessions. The M5 features comfortable but firmer flanges.\n\nStandard Sizing (Both Models):\n\n24mm flange included\n\nThree flange inserts\n: 17mm, 19mm, and 21mm\n\nExtended Sizing:\nThe M5 offers separately-sold 27mm flanges for mothers with larger nipples—an option currently unavailable for the Air 1.\n\nMilk Collector Capacity\n\nAir 1\n: 6 ounces (180ml) with flat, stable base\n\nM5\n: 160ml with rounded base\n\nThe Air 1's larger capacity reduces the frequency of emptying during sessions. Its flat, stable base is a significant advantage, allowing you to place the collector on a desktop after pumping without worrying about it tipping over and spilling\n\nPortability and Discretion\n\nWeight and Dimensions\n\nMomcozy Air 1\n: 260g\n\nMomcozy M5\n: 230g (with all accessories)\n\nDespite the 30g difference, both pumps are lightweight enough for all-day wear under clothing.\n\nM5 Carrying Case\n\nThe M5 includes a \"hard-shell storage bag\" designed to \"keep your pump safe from bumps and scratches\" while \"looking neat too\". It's a stylish, compact case focused on protection and basic transport, in line with the \"Be Fashionable, Be Cozy\" concept.\n\nAir 1 Charging & Carrying Case: Unseen Power\n\nA major highlight of the Air 1 is its advanced charging and carrying case, built for true \"on-the-go convenience\". This \"stylish travel case\" not only stores the pumps but also functions as a powerful portable power bank with \"up to 1800 mAh battery capacity\".\n\nThis \"Unseen Power\" is a key feature, providing enough charge for what can amount to 5 days of battery life or 15 pumping sessions. This all-in-one solution completely eliminates the need to pack separate chargers when traveling and is remarkably smaller than the M5's standard case.\n\nNoise Levels\n\nAir 1\n: ≤45dB (whisper-quiet operation)\n\nM5\n: ≤50dB (relatively quiet)\n\nThe Air 1's exceptional discretion at 45dB makes it ideal for\npumping in professional settings\n, shared offices, or public spaces where privacy is limited. Both pumps operate quietly enough for most environments, but the 5dB difference is noticeable in silent rooms.\n\nBattery Life and Charging Options\n\nMomcozy M5 Charging\n\nThe M5 comes with standard USB Type-C connectivity and can be charged in about 120 minutes. After this is done, it will last for 4-5 pumps (approx. 150 minutes) with each pump lasting 30 minutes.\n\nMomcozy Air 1 Dual Charging Methods\n\nThe Air 1 offers more versatile power management with two charging options:\n\nUSB Type-C cable for traditional charging\n\nMagnetic charging cable for quick, convenient power-ups\n\nThe included charging case doubles as a portable power bank, ensuring you're never caught without battery during critical pumping times—especially valuable for working mothers or frequent travelers.\n\nMaintenance and Care\n\nDaily Cleaning Routine\n\nAdequate cleaning\nis necessary for hygienic purposes and for effective pump functioning. Similar maintenance is required for both pumps, but extra components on Air 1 require extra care.\n\nAfter Each Use:\n\nDisassemble all parts that contact breast milk (flange, diaphragm, valve, milk collector, milk collector back cover if applicable)\n\nRinse immediately with cold water to remove milk residue\n\nWash all parts with warm soapy water using mild dish detergent\n\nUse a dedicated brush to clean valve and diaphragm thoroughly\n\nRinse all components with clean water\n\nAir dry on a clean towel or drying rack—avoid cloth towels that may leave lint\n\nMotor Unit Care\n\nWipe the motor unit with a clean and damp cloth only\n\nNever immerse the motor in water\n\nMake sure all components are fully dried before reassembly\n\nWeekly Sterilization\n\nOnce a week, pump components can be sterilized by one of the following:\n\nBoiling\n: Place parts in boiling water for 5 minutes\n\nSteam sterilizer\n: Follow manufacturer's instructions\n\nMicrowave steam bags\n: Use bags made for storing breast pump components\n\nThe flanges and milk collectors for both models are dishwasher safe (top rack only), but washing by hand will increase their life.\n\nAssembly Instructions\n\nAir 1 Assembly:\n\nPosition the diaphragm on top of your valve\n\nInsert the valve assembly into the flange\n\nAttach the milk collector to the bottom of the flange\n\nSecure the milk collector back cover by twisting clockwise\n\nConnect the assembled flange to the motor unit by aligning and pressing firmly\n\nPower on and select your desired mode\n\nM5 Assembly:\n\nInsert the valve into the flange\n\nAttach the diaphragm over the valve\n\nConnect the milk collector to the flange\n\nAttach the assembled unit to the motor\n\nPower on using the control buttons\n\nPrice and Value Analysis\n\nMomcozy Air 1 vs M5 Price\n\nMomcozy Air 1\n: $369.99\n\nMomcozy M5\n: $199.99\n\nThe $170 price difference reflects the Air 1's premium features: smart app control, professional pumping patterns (Milk Boost™, Milk Relief™, MyFlow™), dual charging methods, quieter operation (45dB vs 50dB), stronger maximum suction (-280 mmHg vs -240 mmHg), and more suction levels (15 vs 9).\n\nValue Considerations\n\nThe M5 is great for frugal mothers looking for affordable wearable pump functionality. Here, you have a great pump with several modes and decent suction power for about half the cost of the Air 1.\n\nThe Air 1 is worth every penny for tech-savvy mothers who appreciate tracking, customization, and professional-level pumping sequences. It is worth investing in for working mothers who require discreet and optimal nursing while on busy work schedules.\n\nWhich Breast Pump Should You Choose\n\nThe\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nis the perfect choice if you value simplicity, reliability, and want a high-quality pump without needing app-based controls. The\n\nMomcozy Air 1\n\nis the premium choice for the mom who is frequently on-the-go, needs to pump in discreet environments, or wants data and customization to optimize her milk supply.\n\n4.7\n\nRated 4.7 out of 5 stars\n\n140\n\nMomcozy Air 1 Ultra-slim Breast Pump\n\n$314.99\n\n$369.99\n\nAdd to Cart\n\nShop Now\n\nChoose the Momcozy M5 When\n\nUpdate\n\nBest-seller M5 is now\nM5 Smart\n!\n\nConnect to the\nMomcozy App\nto track volume and control sessions from your phone.\n\n✓ Smart Tracking\n\n✓ App Control\n\nShop Now\n\nThe M5 is perfect for you if:\n\nYou prefer straightforward, on-pump manual controls and an easy-to-read LED screen.\n\nYou value simplicity and want to \"just pump\" without needing a smartphone or app.\n\nYou have a consistent milk supply and find standard pumping modes are effective for you.\n\nYou primarily pump at home or in comfortable environments where absolute silence isn't your top priority (it's still quiet at ≤50dB).\n\nYou want a durable, \"hard-shell storage bag\" that protects your pump from bumps and scratches.\n\nThe M5 offers everything you need for effective, reliable pumping. It’s a dependable workhorse for moms who prefer a traditional, screen-on-pump experience with the convenience of a wearable design.\n\nChoose the Momcozy Air 1 When\n\nThe Air 1 is the right choice for you if:\n\nYou are a data-driven mom who wants to track pumping history and optimize sessions using app insights.\n\nYou need to pump in very quiet environments, like a shared office or in public, and require whisper-quiet operation (≤45dB).\n\nYou are frequently on-the-go, traveling, or commuting and need the \"Unseen Power\" of its 1800 mAh charging case, which provides up to 5 days of battery life or 15 pumping sessions without needing a wall outlet.\n\nYou face challenges with low supply, stubborn clogs, or engorgement and need stronger suction (up to -280 mmHg) and specialized modes like Milk Boost™ or Milk Relief™.\n\nYou value maximum control and want to create your own personalized pumping rhythms with MyFlow™ Mode.\n\nYou appreciate smart, spill-proof designs, like a flat-base collector that can sit on your desk without tipping over.\n\nBoth pumps are excellent choices. The difference is matching the technology to your lifestyle. The M5 is about simplicity and reliability, while the Air 1 is about advanced power, data, and ultimate portability for a busy, modern routine.\n\nFAQs\n\nIs Air 1 better than M5 Smart?\n\nBetter at slim + case + sensor alerts. Not automatically better at emptying every body. M5 Smart still pulls 285 mmHg on a smaller cup.\n\nIs the M5 in this URL the Smart version?\n\nTreat it as M5 Smart in 2026. The button-only M5 is the older sibling.\n\nAir 1 vs Willow Go?\n\nBoth aim at a low profile. Willow’s app and bags stay in Willow’s world. Air 1 is our slim cup with a wireless case and full-collector alert.\n\nDoes Air 1 have an app?\n\nYes. Sensor-enabled: mode switching and a full-cup 