\nAPP\n\nSize Guide\n\nFAQ\n\nShipping & Delivery\n\nReturn & Exchange\n\nCommunity Discount\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nContact Us\n\nBreastfeeding\n\nMomcozy Air 1 vs M9: Which Wearable Breast Pump is Right for You?\n\nBy : Momcozy Care Team\n\nLast updated :\nAugust 10, 2026\n\nTable of Contents\n\nDesign and Build Quality\n\nFlange System and Compatibility\n\nMilk Collection and Storage\n\nSmart Features and Pumping Modes\n\nSuction Power and Performance\n\nPortability and Discretion\n\nBattery Life and Charging Options\n\nCleaning and Maintenance\n\nPrice Comparison and Value\n\nWhich Pump Should You Choose?\n\nFinal Thoughts\n\nShow All\n\nChoosing the right breast pump can significantly impact your breastfeeding journey. Momcozy offers two popular wearable models: the Air 1 and the M9, both providing hands-free convenience for busy moms. While they share smart app control features, they differ in suction strength, noise levels, portability, and pricing. This comprehensive comparison will help you choose the pump that best fits your needs.\n\nDesign and Build Quality\n\nOverall Design Comparison\n\nThe\n\nMomcozy Air 1\n\nand\n\nM9\n\nshare a similar aesthetic with their distinctive tear-drop shape and flat base for stability, but differ in several important design aspects. The Air 1 features a unique transparent top that allows you to monitor milk flow in real-time without interrupting your pumping session, and adjust nipple placement for optimal comfort and efficiency —a thoughtful design element that provides visual feedback and peace of mind. The Air 1 is available in one color variant and measures 125mm x 110mm x 61mm, making it notably thinner than the M9. The M9 offers two color variants and measures 127mm x 109mm x 77mm, providing a slightly thicker profile but maintaining excellent portability.\n\nMomcozy Air 1 Ultra-slim Breast Pump\n\n$314.99 USD\n\n$369.99 USD\n\nUltra-slim\n\nWireless Charging\n\nEffortless Alignment\n\nSmart App Control\n\nMomcozy Mobile Flow™ Hands-Free Breast Pump | M9\n\nFrom\n$159.99 USD\n\nHigh Efficiency\n\nExpert-Tuned Rhythms\n\nAPP Control\n\nLong Battery\n\nAssembly Components\n\nThe Air 1 consists of 6 parts: motor, flange, diaphragm, valve, milk collector, and milk collector back cover, plus a USB Type-C cable, magnetic charging cable, and flange cover.\n\nThe M9 has a simpler assembly with only 5 parts, along with a USB Type-C cable and flange cover. While the Air 1 has one additional component, both models remain intuitive to assemble. First-time users should consult the user guide to ensure proper setup, as correct assembly is essential for effective pumping performance.\n\nDisplay and Controls\n\nThe display systems differ significantly between models. The M9 features a full LED screen that displays pumping information clearly, making it easy to monitor your session at a glance. In contrast, the Air 1 uses a simple indicator light to show operating status, offering a more minimalist approach.\n\nFor pump direction selection, the M9 includes a convenient toggle button that allows you to select between left or right breast. The Air 1 takes a different approach with clear L or R markings directly on the pump body to indicate which breast each unit is designed for.\n\nFlange System and Compatibility\n\nFlange Technology\n\nBoth pumps come with a 24mm flange and three flange inserts (17mm, 19mm, and 21mm) as standard, accommodating most mothers' needs. However, their flange technologies differ. The M9 utilizes the innovative DoubleFit™ flange system, while the Air 1 features a soft, flexible flange design that adapts comfortably to your body.\n\nSize Options for Different Needs\n\nFor mothers with larger nipples, the M9 offers 27mm flanges sold separately, providing additional sizing flexibility that ensures a proper fit for every body type. This expanded sizing option makes the M9 particularly suitable for mothers who require larger flange sizes.\n\nMilk Collection and Storage\n\nCollector Capacity\n\nThe Air 1 boasts a larger milk collection capacity at 6 ounces (180ml) compared to the M9's 150ml capacity. This additional capacity can be particularly beneficial during longer pumping sessions or for mothers with higher milk output, reducing the need for mid-session interruptions.\n\nStorage Convenience\n\nBoth models feature a flat-base milk collector design for stability. A key practical difference is that the M9 includes a lid for its milk collector, allowing you to store breast milk directly in the collector after pumping—perfect for quick storage between sessions. The Air 1 lacks this lid, requiring you to transfer milk to separate storage containers after each pumping session.\n\nSmart Features and Pumping Modes\n\nApp Control Capabilities\n\nBoth the Momcozy Air 1 and M9 share the same smart app control feature, allowing you to sync the pump with your smartphone. Through the Momcozy app, you can adjust pumping settings, track your pumping history, and access advanced features that enhance your pumping experience. This smart technology integration provides convenience and detailed insights into your breastfeeding journey.\n\nThree Core Pumping Modes\n\nBoth models offer three fundamental pumping modes designed to mimic natural breastfeeding patterns.\nStimulation mode\nuses a quick and short sucking pattern to initiate\nmilk letdown\n, helping your body prepare for expression.\nExpression mode\nemploys a slower, deeper sucking pattern for efficient milk extraction once letdown occurs.\nMixed mode\ncombines both approaches, starting with quick stimulation before transitioning to slower, longer suction for comprehensive milk expression throughout your session.\n\nProfessional Recommended Patterns\n\nBeyond the standard modes, both models provide two specialized patterns accessible exclusively through the Momcozy app.\nMilk Boost™\nis designed for mothers looking to enhance milk production, using evidence-based patterns to encourage increased supply.\nMilk Relief™\ngently eases discomfort and expresses milk for mothers experiencing engorgement or enlarged breasts, providing targeted relief when you need it most.\n\nPersonalized MyFlow™ Mode\n\nThe MyFlow™ feature allows you to customize your pumping experience through the Momcozy app. You can adjust any of the three regular modes (stimulation, expression, or mixed) and fine-tune intensity levels to create a personalized pattern that optimizes your comfort, efficiency, and milk production based on your unique needs and body's response.\n\nSuction Power and Performance\n\nMaximum Suction Strength\n\nWhile both pumps offer 15 suction levels with incremental adjustments, their performance ranges differ slightly. The M9 delivers a maximum suction power of -300mmHg, slightly stronger than the Air 1's -280mmHg maximum, making it ideal for mothers who need more powerful expression.\n\nAir 1 Specifications\n\nThe Air 1 offers comprehensive suction and cycle speed ranges across all three pumping modes, with incremental adjustments to help you find your optimal comfort level.\n\nMode\n\nVacuum Range\n\nCycle Speed\n\nStimulation\n\n-67.5mmHg to -172.5mmHg (+15mmHg increments)\n\n54-90 cycles/min (+2 cycles/min increments)\n\nExpression\n\n-105mmHg to -280mmHg\n\n25-60 cycles/min (+2 cycles/min increments)\n\nMixed\n\n-67.5mmHg to -280mmHg\n\n46-84 cycles/min (+2 cycles/min increments)\n\nThese specifications demonstrate the Air 1's versatility in adapting to different letdown patterns and milk flow preferences.\n\nM9 Specifications\n\nThe M9 delivers slightly higher maximum suction power, particularly beneficial for mothers who require stronger expression.\n\nMode\n\nVacuum Range\n\nCycle Speed\n\nStimulation\n\n-67mmHg to -172mmHg\n\n62-90 cycles/min (+2 cycles/min increments)\n\nExpression\n\n-105mmHg to -300mmHg\n\n26-60 cycles/min (+2 cycles/min increments)\n\nMixed\n\n-105mmHg to -300mmHg\n\n50-85 cycles/min (+2 cycles/min increments)\n\nWith its maximum -300mmHg suction in both expression and mixed modes, the M9 provides powerful performance for efficient milk extraction.\n\nPortability and Discretion\n\nWeight and Dimensions\n\nPortability is especially important for mothers who express milk in their office or are constantly on the road. The Momcozy Air 1 is much lighter, weighing only 260g, making it easier to transport with you throughout your day. The M9 is slightly heavier but only tips the scale at 302g with accessories.\n\nThe Air 1 is much thinner (61mm compared to 77mm), which makes it easier to conceal under your clothing. This means that it is much more discreet for nursing mothers when\nused in a working\nor public environment.\n\nCarrying and Storage Cases\n\nBoth models come with carrying cases for convenient transport and storage, though they differ in functionality. The\nM9\nincludes a standard carrying case designed to accommodate the pump and its accessories securely. The\nAir 1\nfeatures a dual-purpose charging and carrying case—not only does it store your pump, but it also functions as a charging station for ultimate convenience. Notably, the Air 1's case is more compact than the M9's, offering enhanced portability for mothers who prioritize minimal bulk in their daily carry.\n\nNoise Level Performance\n\nDiscretion matters when pumping in shared spaces like offices, cafes, or public areas. The M9 operates at an impressively quiet ≤42dB, making it one of the quieter wearable pumps available and comparable to a quiet library. The Air 1 runs at ≤45dB, still maintaining whisper-quiet operation that allows for discreet pumping without drawing attention. Both models enable you to pump confidently in various environments, though the M9 holds a slight edge in ultra-quiet performance for the most noise-sensitive situations.\n\nBattery Life and Charging Options\n\nCharging Methods\n\nThe M9 and Air 1 take different approaches to charging convenience. The M9 uses a straightforward USB Type-C charging cable with a protective dust plug covering the charging port, preventing debris accumulation and maintaining hygiene between charges.\n\nThe Air 1 offers more flexibility with two charging methods. It can be charged via the standard USB Type-C cable for direct connection or through a convenient magnetic charging cable that attaches easily to the pump. This dual-charging capability provides added convenience, especially for mothers who prefer the ease of magnetic connection or need to charge on the go without fumbling with cables.\n\nBattery Performance\n\nWhen it comes to battery life, the M9 delivers reliable performance. After a full charge, which takes approximately 150 minutes, the M9 can power through 4-5 pumping sessions, totaling about 150 minutes of operation time based on 30-minute sessions. This capacity ensures you can complete multiple pumping sessions throughout the day or even over a couple of days without needing to recharge constantly.\n\nWhile specific battery performance data for the Air 1 wasn't provided, its dual-charging system offers practical advantages for busy mothers who value charging convenience and flexibility in their daily routine, ensuring you're never caught without power.\n\nCleaning and Maintenance\n\nDaily Cleaning Routine\n\nProper cleaning and maintenance\nare critical. Whether it is the M9 or Air 1, both pumps require the same cleaning instructions. After every pumping session, all components that come into contact with your expressed milk need to be taken apart. These components include the flange, diaphragm, valve, milk collector, and finally, for Air 1, the milk collector's back cover.\n\nThese components should be rinsed immediately with cold water to prevent any milk residues from drying. These components should then be washed with soap and warm water. Be sure to pay particular attention to areas such as crevices and diaphragms. Use a brush if necessary. These components should then be rinsed with cold water to wash any soap residue out. They should then be dried with a towel.\n\nMotor Care\n\nNever submerge the motor unit in water—simply wipe it with a damp cloth to keep it clean. The motor units of both pumps require minimal maintenance but should be kept clean and dry. Wipe the exterior regularly with a slightly damp cloth and ensure the charging ports remain free from debris. For the M9, use the dust plug to protect the USB Type-C port when not charging.\n\nDisinfection Guidelines\n\nPeriodic\ndisinfection\nprovides an extra layer of protection, especially important for newborns or babies with compromised immune systems. You can sterilize pump parts using boiling water (submerge for 5 minutes), a\nsteam sterilizer\n, or microwave steam bags following manufacturer instructions. Disinfect at least once daily, or more frequently if your healthcare provider recommends. Always ensure parts are completely dry before reassembly to prevent bacterial growth and maintain optimal pump performance.\n\nPrice Comparison and Value\n\nThe difference in price for these models is related to their features and design. The\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nis priced at $269.99\n(Black Friday Special: $159.99\n). This makes it relatively affordable without affecting smart features, suction power, and performance.\n\nThe\n\nMomcozy Air 1\n\nis priced at $369.99, which is a significant investment but comes with added benefits such as improved portability due to its thinner design, bigger 180ml milk storage, multiple modes for charging with magnets, and improved discretion.\n\nMomcozy Mobile Flow™ Hands-Free Breast Pump | M9\n\nFrom\n$159.99 USD\n\nHigh Efficiency\n\nExpert-Tuned Rhythms\n\nAPP Control\n\nLong Battery\n\nMomcozy Air 1 Ultra-slim Breast Pump\n\n$314.99 USD\n\n$369.99 USD\n\nUltra-slim\n\nWireless Charging\n\nEffortless Alignment\n\nSmart App Control\n\nThe difference in price by $100 can be considered acceptable based on your personal needs and preferences. If you require utmost portability, multiple charging options, and a slim design, then you will greatly appreciate what the Air 1 offers. On the other hand, if you're looking for a vacuum cleaner with outstanding performance capabilities, strong suction power, interaction with smart apps, LED screens, and convenient features for a lower price tag, then I believe you would greatly appreciate what the M9 has to offer.\n\nWhich Pump Should You Choose?\n\nBest for Ultimate Portability: Momcozy Air 1\n\nIf you value a slim, discreet, and super-portable pump that can easily fit your busy schedule, then you should choose Momcozy Air 1.\nMomcozy Air 1\nis perfect for working mothers who pump in their office setting or for mothers who travel or have busy schedules.\n\nIts significantly thinner profile (61mm vs 77mm) makes it less noticeable under clothing, providing confidence when pumping in professional settings. The larger 180ml milk collector capacity means fewer interruptions during longer pumping sessions, while the dual charging system—including convenient magnetic charging—provides flexibility for travel and daily use. The lighter 260g weight and compact charging case make it easy to carry everywhere without adding bulk to your bag.\n\nIf you value maximum discretion, portability, and charging convenience combined with smart technology and effective pumping performance, the Air 1 is your best choice.\n\nBest for Power and Value: Momcozy M9\n\nChoose the\nMomcozy M9\nif you want a powerful, feature-rich pump with the strongest suction capability (-300mmHg) at a more accessible price point. With its LED screen for easy monitoring of settings and session progress, quieter operation (≤42dB) for maximum discretion, and the practical milk collector lid for direct storage, the M9 offers convenience and efficiency in one package.\n\nThe toggle button for selecting pump direction provides intuitive control, while the availability of 27mm flanges (sold separately) accommodates mothers with larger nipples who need proper sizing. The M9 is perfect for experienced moms who understand their pumping needs and want precise, customizable settings through smart app control—all while balancing career and breastfeeding efficiently without the premium price tag.\n\nIf strong suction power, visual display monitoring, and excellent value for money are your priorities, the M9 delivers exceptional performance at a budget-friendly price.\n\nFinal Thoughts\n\nBoth the Momcozy Air 1 and M9 represent excellent\nwearable breast pump\noptions with smart app control, multiple pumping modes, and hands-free convenience that supports modern mothers' busy lifestyles. Your choice ultimately depends on your specific needs, priorities, and daily routine.\n\nThe Air 1 excels in portability and discretion with its slimmer design, larger milk capacity, lighter weight, and dual charging flexibility—ideal for mothers constantly on the move who need a pump that disappears under clothing and travels effortlessly. The M9 offers powerful performance with its maximum -300mmHg suction, LED display for easy monitoring, quieter operation, practical storage features with the milk collector lid, and all at a more budget-friendly price point.\n\nThink about your personal daily activities, your common pump site environments, your cost considerations, and your personal preferences. Whether you select Momcozy's ultra-portable Air 1 pump or choose to purchase one of their powerful M9 pumps, rest assured that all models bring you Momcozy's smart technology, performance, and quality.\n\nDisclaimer\n\nThe information provided in this article is for general informational purposes only and does not constitute medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Always seek the advice of your physician or other qualified health provider regarding any medical condition. Momcozy is not responsible for any consequences arising from the use of this content.\n\nRelated articles\n\n22\n\nSep\n\nBreastfeeding\n\nUsing a Nursing Pillow With a Reflux Baby: The Safe Ans