Guide\n\nFAQ\n\nShipping & Delivery\n\nReturn & Exchange\n\nCommunity Discount\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nContact Us\n\nMomcare\n\nMomcozy M5 vs M9: Which Breast Pump Is Right for You?\n\nBy : Momcozy Care Team\n\nLast updated :\nAugust 10, 2026\n\nTable of Contents\n\nSmart Features: M9's App Control vs M5's Manual Operation\n\nWhat Are the Design Differences Between the M5 and M9?\n\nPerformance Comparison: M9's Advanced Motor vs M5's Basic Functionality\n\nBattery Life: M5 vs M9 Runtime and Charging Differences\n\nPortability: M5's Lightweight Design vs M9's Premium Travel Features\n\nCleaning Guide: M5 and M9 Maintenance Made Simple\n\nPrice Comparison: Is the M9's Higher Cost Worth It?\n\nWhich Pump Fits Your Needs? Momcozy M5 vs M9\n\nChoose Your Perfect Momcozy Pump Today — M5 or M9?\n\nShow All\n\nThe right breast pump can make all the difference for new moms, and when\ncomparing the Momcozy M5 vs M9\n, there are several key differences to consider. The M5 comes with a lightweight design that's easy to use right out of the box, which is perfect for first-time moms. The M9 has stronger suctions (up to -300mmHg) and higher adjustable levels (1-15 levels). These models differ not just in tech features but also in their design, suction power, and milk collection systems.\n\nUpdate\n\nBest-seller M5 is now\nM5 Smart\n!\n\nConnect to the\nMomcozy App\nto track volume and control sessions from your phone.\n\n✓ Smart Tracking\n\n✓ App Control\n\nShop Now\n\nSmart Features: M9's App Control vs M5's Manual Operation\n\nThe\nM9 Mobile Flow™ Hands-Free Breast Pump\nconnects to your phone, letting you adjust settings and track pumping sessions through an app. The\nM5 Wearable Breast Pump\nkeeps things simple with buttons right on the pump that you press to change settings. This basic difference affects how you'll use each breast pump every day.\n\nMomcozy Mobile Flow™ Hands-Free Breast Pump | M9\n\nFrom\n$159.99 USD\n\nHigh Efficiency\n\nExpert-Tuned Rhythms\n\nAPP Control\n\nLong Battery\n\nMomcozy M5: Manual Operation\n\nThe\nMomcozy M5\nalso does things the simple way, with its manual-only model that most moms adore for how easy it is. All of it is in front of you on the device itself, with buttons you can physically press to control modes and suction strengths as you pump. Without app connectivity, the M5 won't track or retain your pumping data, but it also means not having to deal with device pairing or phone charging before pumping. The M5's direct control system is plug-and-play right out of the box, so it is an option that is convenient for moms who simply want a no-gadget pumping experience with no need for a learning curve.\n\nMomcozy M9: Smart App Control\n\nThe M9 breast pump provides you with options that are in tune with your style. You can simply use the buttons on the pump itself – a wonderful option if you prefer an uncomplicated method without extra technology. Many moms like this hassle-free option for quick and convenient pumping sessions. Or if you're the type who likes to monitor, sync with your phone via the Momcozy app. This enables you to make adjustments without having to lift the pump while in use, and monitors your pumping sessions over time. Technologically oriented mothers will enjoy innovative features like Milk Boost™ to increase output, Milk Relief™ if you feel self-conscious, and the customized MyFlow™ Mode through which you can create a pumping routine that feels perfect for you. Whether you like to keep it simple or enjoy having your pumping data at hand, the M9 accommodates you.\n\nWhat Are the Design Differences Between the M5 and M9?\n\nBoth the M5 and M9 breast pumps look and feel different while in use. The M5 breast pump is curved and lighter, while the M9 breast pump has a flat bottom to allow it to stand up on its own. The M5's lighter, simpler design weighs less in the bra, but the design of the M9 allows it to be easily set down between uses and not leak milk. The M9 features independent milk collectors, so you don’t need to wash or pour out the milk immediately after pumping.\n\nOverall Design\n\nThe Momcozy M5 and M9 breast pumps also differ significantly in design, which affects both aesthetics and function. The M5 features a traditional semi-circular design that comfortably curves against the breast, while the M9 comes in a modern tear-drop shape that has a flat base for it to rest on when not in use.\n\nFeature\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nShape\n\nSemi-circular\n\nTear-drop with flat base\n\nColors Available\n\n4 options (Cozy Red, Lilac, Quill Grey, Mint)\n\n2 options (Cozy Red, Quill Grey)\n\nSize\n\nCompact, slightly smaller profile\n\nSlightly larger with stand-up capability\n\nWeight\n\n230g (8.1 oz)\n\n302g (10.6 oz)\n\nParts Breakdown\n\nBoth the M5 and M9 are designed with simplicity in mind, featuring just five main components that are easy to assemble and clean.\n\nBoth models include these 5 parts:\n\nBreast shield/flange\n\nConnector\n\nMotor unit\n\nMilk collectors made from Tritan™\n\nSilicone valve\n\nM5 Smart Breast Pump Replacement Parts\n\nFrom\n$6.99 USD\n\nFlange System\n\nThe flanges on both Momcozy models are engineered with mom's comfort as a priority. Both the M5 and M9 feature the same innovative 105° angle design that better mimics a baby's natural latch.\n\nFeature\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nMaterial\n\nSoft silicone\n\nCombination of hard and soft silicone\n\nStandard Flange Sizes\n\n24mm\n\n24mm\n\nFlange Slope\n\n105-degree slope\n\n105-degree slope\n\nDesign Philosophy\n\nMimics natural curvature of baby's mouth\n\nTraditional pump design\n\nSmaller Inserts\n\n3 flange inserts (17mm/19mm/21mm)\n\n3 flange inserts (17mm/19mm/21mm)\n\nDouble Fit Flange\n\nYes\n\nYes\n\nThe M9 has a special DoubleFit™ Flange that combines soft silicone and hard silicone. The part touching your breast is soft for comfort, while the part connecting to the milk bowl is firm to prevent leaks. Momcozy's tests show this design enhances pumping efficiency by 28.2%, and increase leak-proof performance by 10%. The M5, on the other hand, uses only soft silicone throughout its flange.\n\nMilk Collection System\n\nThe M9 features milk collectors made from Tritan™—a BPA-free, medical-grade material known for its durability, safety, and resistance to odors and stains, making it ideal for repeated use in daily pumping routines.\n\nFeature\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nCapacity\n\n160ml (5.4 oz)\n\n150ml (5.1 oz)\n\nDesign\n\nRounded bottom design\n\nFlat-based container with lid\n\nStorage\n\nNo integrated lid\n\nIncludes lid for temporary storage\n\nStability\n\nMay tip over when set down\n\nCan stand upright on flat surface\n\nThe M9 includes four milk collection cups in total – two standard plus two extras. What's really convenient is that these cups have flat bottoms, so once you're done pumping, you can simply snap on the lid and pop them straight in the fridge. The M5's cups have rounded bottoms that won't stand up on their own, so you'll need to transfer your milk to storage containers right after pumping.\n\nControl Interface\n\nThe control panels on each model reflect their different technological capabilities, with the M9 offering more advanced features.\n\nFeature\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nLED Screen\n\nBasic display\n\nLarger, clearer display\n\nScreen Information\n\nMode\n\nSuction level\n\nBattery life\n\nBuilt-in timer\n\nMode\n\nSuction level\n\nBattery life\n\nBuilt-in timer\n\nApp Integration\n\nNone\n\nYes (Momcozy app)\n\nApp Control\n\nNo\n\nYes (start, pause, stop via app)\n\nSession Tracking\n\nNo\n\nYes (records pumping sessions)\n\nMilk Output Tracking\n\nNo\n\nYes (tracks milk output)\n\nDirection Control\n\nNo dedicated button\n\nYes - has a left/right switch button to easily track which breast you're pumping\n\nThe M9's enhanced interface supports its smart capabilities, while the M5 offers a simpler, more straightforward user experience that many moms find intuitive and easy to use right from the start.\n\nMomcozy Mobile Flow™ Hands-Free Breast Pump | M9\n\nFrom\n$159.99 USD\n\nHigh Efficiency\n\nExpert-Tuned Rhythms\n\nAPP Control\n\nLong Battery\n\nM9 Wearable Breast Pump Replacement Parts\n\nFrom\n$9.99 USD\n\nPerformance Comparison: M9's Advanced Motor vs M5's Basic Functionality\n\nThe M9 breast pump contains a newer and more adjustable motor with more features to help you express milk more efficiently. It has 15 suction levels along with special modes for maximizing milk output, whereas the M5 breast pump gives only nine general levels with none of the other features. If you tend to pump lots or experience challenges with milk flow, these differences between breast pumps can matter.\n\nMotor Technology\n\nThe motor is the heart of any breast pump, and Momcozy has come a long way between these two products. M5 employs Momcozy's 1st generation motor, which provides reliable performance for day-to-day pumping needs. M9, however, is a significant upgrade with its 3rd generation motor technology, providing better power efficiency and quieter operation. This new motor enables the M9's enhanced functionality without sacrificing battery life compared to the M5 in spite of added features.\n\nPumping Modes\n\nBoth pumps offer versatile pumping options, though the M9 provides more specialized patterns for different needs.\n\nPumping Modes\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nStandard Modes\n\n✓ Stimulation\n\n✓ Expression\n\n✓ Mixed\n\n✓ Stimulation\n\n✓ Expression\n\n✓ Mixed\n\nProfessional Patterns\n\n❌ Not available\n\n✓ Milk Boost™ (enhances production)\n\n✓ Milk Relief™ (reduces engorgement)\n\nCustomizable Settings\n\n❌ Not available\n\n✓ MyFlow™ mode (create personalized pumping patterns)\n\nMomcozy Mobile Flow™ Hands-Free Breast Pump | M9\n\nFrom\n$159.99 USD\n\nHigh Efficiency\n\nExpert-Tuned Rhythms\n\nAPP Control\n\nLong Battery\n\nSuction Power\n\nThe suction capabilities between these two models show notable differences in both range and precision control.\n\nSuction Features\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nSuction Levels\n\n9 levels\n\n15 levels\n\nMax Vacuum Strength\n\n280 mmHg\n\n300 mmHg\n\nCycle Speed Range\n\n26-60 cycles/min\n\n26-70 cycles/min\n\nFine-Tuning\n\nMore noticeable jumps between levels\n\nSmoother transitions between levels\n\nIndependent Control\n\nCan only adjust both sides together\n\nCan control left and right sides independently\n\nThe M9's expanded suction range and additional levels allow for more precise control, which can be especially beneficial for moms with sensitive tissue or those who need to experiment to find their ideal settings. The M5 still provides effective suction for most users but with fewer adjustment options.\n\nBattery Life: M5 vs M9 Runtime and Charging Differences\n\nBoth breast pumps take approximately the same amount of time on a charge—2-2.5 hours or 4-5 pumping sessions. The M5 breast pump is charged faster (2 hours) than the M9 breast pump (3 hours), but either will get you through a whole day of pumping before needing to be plugged back in.\n\nBattery Runtime\n\nBoth the M5 and M9 Momcozy breast pumps are equipped with impressive battery life to keep up with busy moms in their day. Both pumps are equipped with rechargeable lithium-ion batteries that are able to sustain a consistent stream of power during multiple pumping sessions. With their batteries fully charged, both products tend to be able to sustain sufficient power to support 4-5 full pumping sessions or around 2-2.5 hours of continuous use. This allows most mothers to get through an entire day of pumping before needing to recharge, so these pumps are feasible options for working mothers or those who tend to be mobile.\n\nMomcozy M5 vs M9 Breast Pump Technical Comparison\n\nFeature\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nSuction Levels\n\n9 levels\n\n15 levels\n\nVacuum Range (Stimulation Mode)\n\n-52 to-113 (+5) mmHg\n\n-67 to -172 mmHg\n\nVacuum Range (Expression Mode)\n\n-105 to-240 (+5) mmHg\n\n-105 to -300 mmHg\n\nVacuum Range (Mixed Mode)\n\n-52 to -240 (+5) mmHg\n\n-105 to -300 mmHg\n\nCycle Speed (Stimulation Mode)\n\n50-120 cycles/min\n\n62-90 cycles/min\n\nCycle Speed (Expression Mode)\n\n23-57 cycles/min\n\n26-66 cycles/min\n\nCycle Speed (Mixed Mode)\n\n6-16 cycles/min\n\n50-85 cycles/min\n\nOverall Power\n\nLess powerful\n\nMore powerful\n\nCharging Protection Features\n\nThe M9 introduces thoughtful enhancements to protect the pump's internal components. Most notably, it includes a built-in dust plug for the charging port, which helps prevent dust, lint, and moisture from entering the USB-C connection. This small but significant feature helps extend the life of the charging port and reduces the risk of charging issues over time. The M5 does not include this protective feature, leaving the charging port exposed when not in use.\n\nBoth models feature smart charging protection to prevent overcharging, with automatic shutoff once the battery reaches full capacity. They also include battery level indicators on their displays, allowing you to monitor remaining power at a glance and plan your charging schedule accordingly.\n\nMomcozy Mobile Flow™ Hands-Free Breast Pump | M9\n\nFrom\n$159.99 USD\n\nHigh Efficiency\n\nExpert-Tuned Rhythms\n\nAPP Control\n\nLong Battery\n\nPortability: M5's Lightweight Design vs M9's Premium Travel Features\n\nBoth the M5 and M9 come with carrying cases, so you can take either pump wherever you need to go. If you're looking for something super light, go with the M5. It won't weigh you down as much during those longer pumping sessions.\n\nThe M9 is a bit heavier, but it makes up for it with a nicer case that has separate compartments to keep all your pumping stuff organized. Plus, it runs quieter, which is great if you need to pump around others or during meetings.\n\nPortability Features\n\nWhen choosing a wearable breast pump, portability becomes a crucial factor for moms who are frequently on the move. The Momcozy M5 and M9 were both designed with mobility in mind, though they differ in several key aspects that affect their day-to-day convenience. While both models offer the freedom of wireless pumping, their weight, noise levels, and carrying options create distinct user experiences that might influence your preference.\n\nFeature\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nWeight\n\n230g (8.1 oz)\n\n280g (9.9 oz)\n\nSize Dimensions\n\n128mm X 117mm X 74mm\n\n127mm X 109mm X 77mm\n\nNoise Level\n\n<=50dB (whisper quiet)\n\n<=48dB (ultra-quiet)\n\nWeight Comparison\n\nThe Momcozy M5 breast pump weighs just 230g (8.1 oz), noticeably lighter than the M9 at 280g (9.9 oz). The M9's slightly higher weight comes from its stronger motor and extra features, which provide better performance during your typical 30-minute pumping sessions. While the M9 is heavier due to its stronger motor and extra features, it offers a teardrop shape that better matches the natural curve of the breast, making it more discreet and less visible under clothing.\n\nNoise Levels\n\nBoth pumps are quiet, but the M9 is even more so. The M5 is <=50dB (a gentle whisper), which is fine for office use or\nnight pumping\nsessions without disturbing your baby. The M9's upgraded motor quiets it down to <=48dB, making it an ultra-quiet device that's hardly audible in typical environments. This makes the M9 perfect for mothers who pump in open areas or at work.\n\nCarrying Options and Travel Features\n\nBoth the M5 and M9 come with dust covers that keep dirt off the flanges when you're not using them. They also include carrying bags to hold all your pump parts in one place. These make it simple to take your pump anywhere - to work, on trips, or around your home. The dust covers help keep the parts that touch your skin clean between uses.\n\nCleaning Guide: M5 and M9 Maintenance Made Simple\n\nEach of the breast pumps comes apart in the same way for washing, four large pieces and a dust cover to clean with each use. M9 breast pumps also include milk collector caps. If you use the cap, remember to wash it as well. Rinse your parts with the breast pump straight away, wash them in soapy water, and let them air dry completely.\n\nParts That Require Cleaning\n\nBoth Momcozy M5 and M9 pumps focus a lot on hygiene and convenience, with both sharing almost the same breakdown of parts that require regular cleaning. The best thing is that with both pumps, the motor unit (the electronic component) never comes in contact with breast milk itself and therefore does not require cleaning—wipe it with a moist cloth as and when required.\n\nComponents Requiring Cleaning\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nBreast shield/flange\n\n✓\n\n✓\n\nSilicone Diaphragm\n\n✓\n\n✓\n\nDuckbill Valve\n\n✓\n\n✓\n\nCollection container/bottle\n\n✓\n\n✓\n\nMilk collector lid/cap\n\nNo\n\n✓ (Included)\n\nDust Cover\n\n✓ (Included)\n\n✓ (Included)\n\nMotor unit\n\nNo washing (wipe only)\n\nNo washing (wipe only)\n\nRecommended Cleaning Procedures\n\nMomcozy recommends the same thorough cleaning protocol for both the M5 and M9 pump parts that come into contact with breast milk:\n\nDaily Cleaning (After Each Use):\n\nDisassemble all milk-contact parts\n(flange, silicone diaphragm, valve, and milk collector)\n\nRinse immediately after use\nwith cool water to remove milk residue\n\nWash thoroughly\nwith warm, soapy water using a dedicated brush (sold separately or use a clean\nbottle brush\n)\n\nRinse completely\nwith clean water until all soap residue is removed\n\nAir dry\non a clean paper towel or drying rack\n\nWipe the motor unit\nwith a slightly damp cloth if necessary (never submerge)\n\nBasic Cleaning Instructions:\n\nM5 Breast Pump:\n\nFor parts that touch milk (silicone parts, collection bottles):\n\n1. Rinse under running water to remove milk residue\n\n2. Wash in a dedicated baby basin with soap and warm water (40-60°C)\n\n3. Scrub with a clean brush used only for baby items\n\n4. Rinse thoroughly and air-dry on a clean towel\n\n5. Disinfect daily after cleaning (avoid microwave or UV sterilizers)\n\nWarning\n: Always clean manually. Don't use antibacterial or abrasive cleaning agents as they may damage the parts.\n\nM9 Breast Pump:\n\nFor the main unit shell:\n\n1. Wash hands with hand sanitizer before starting\n\n2. Wipe the main unit and charging cable with a clean soft cloth\n\n3. Use 70% isopropyl alcohol wipes until no visible dirt remains\n\n4. Let dry at room temperature for 10 minutes\n\n5. For disinfection, dampen a soft cloth with 70% isopropanol and wipe for 3 minutes\n\n6. Let dry for another 10 minutes at room temperature\n\nImportant Note:\nFor both models, always allow all parts to completely air dry before reassembly to prevent mold growth. Store dry parts in a clean, sealed container between uses.\n\nEase of Assembly\n\nBoth the M5 and M9 feature a user-friendly design with minimal parts, making assembly quick and straightforward for busy parents.\n\nAssembly Feature\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nNumber of Parts to Assemble\n\n5 core components\n\n5 core components\n\nAverage Assembly Time\n\nUnder 30 seconds\n\nUnder 30 seconds\n\nFlange Sizes\n\nEasy interchangeability\n\nEasy interchangeability\n\nTroubleshooting Guide\n\nBasic diagram in manual\n\nEnhanced diagram in manual guide\n\nM5 Breast Pump Assembly\n\nPrepare\n: Wash your hands thoroughly with soap and water. Ensure all parts that contact milk or breasts have been cleaned and disinfected.\n\nInspect\n: Check all components for cracks, chips, tears, or discoloration before assembly. Do not use damaged parts.\n\nAttach diaphragm\n: Connect the diaphragm to the milk collector, applying gentle pressure around the edges until properly sealed.\n\nInsert valve\n: Push the valve carefully into the flange, making sure there are no gaps.\n\nConnect flange\n: Align the flange with the milk collector so the patterns overlap. Press down firmly with your thumbs to secure it around the rim.\n\nFinal assembly\n: Connect the pump motor to the milk collector assembly.\n\nYour M5 breast pump is now ready to use.\n\nM9 Breast Pump Assembly\n\nPrepare\n: Wash your hands thoroughly with soap and water. Ensure all parts that contact milk or breasts have been cleaned and disinfected.\n\nInspect\n: Check all components for cracks, chips, tears, or discoloration before assembly. Do not use damaged parts.\n\nAssemble milk bowl\n: Rotate the milk bowl in the direction of the lock icon at the mouth of the bottle.\n\nAttach flange\n: Fasten the flange to the mouth of the bottle and connect it with the milk collector.\n\nFinal assembly\n: Connect the main unit to the assembled flange.\n\nYour M9 breast pump is now ready to use.\n\nImportant\n: For both models, allow disinfected parts to cool completely if you've used boiling water, and avoid touching the inside of any milk collection parts.\n\nPrice Comparison: Is the M9's Higher Cost Worth It?\n\nThe M9 breast pump costs $70 more than the M5 ($269.99 vs $199.99 for double pumps). This extra money gets you app control, more pumping options, quieter operation. Whether it's worth it depends on\nhow often you use your breast pump\nand if you'll actually use these extra features.\n\nPrice Points\n\nThe Momcozy M5 and M9 represent different price tiers within the wearable breast pump market, with a notable difference in their investment levels:\n\nModel\n\nRegular Price\n\nTypical Sale Price\n\nBundle Options\n\nMomcozy M5\n\n$199.99\n\n$159.99 - $179.99\n\nSingle pump: $119.99\n\nDouble pump: $199.99\n\nMomcozy M9\n\n$269.99\n\n$229.99 - $249.99\n\nSingle pump: $159.99\n\nDouble pump: $269.99\n\nWhat Does the Price Difference Get You?\n\nThe $70 price difference between the models reflects several enhanced features in the M9:\n\nAdvanced 3rd generation motor\n(vs. 1st generation in the M5)\n\nAdditional pumping\n\npatterns\nincluding Milk Boost™, Milk Relief™, and customizable MyFlow™\n\nThe M9 delivers stronger suction\nat 300mmHg maximum, while 