ected the ideal pumping rhythm — a balanced blend of gentle suction and natural frequency. This smart rhythm not only feels comfortable but also helps boost your milk supply, making every pumping session more effective and pleasant.\n\n*Tested in the Momcozy R&D lab. Battery life varies depending on usage and settings.\n\n2nd Gen Motor, Strong Suction\n\nThe 2nd gen motor boasts a powerful suction of 295 mmHg, offering three modes and nine suction settings to efficiently assist you in expressing milk.\n\nDiscreet Design for Confident Pumping\n\nInspired by extensive ergonomic research and precise molding, the Mobile Style™ features a sleek, streamlined design that stays nearly invisible under your clothes. No more unwanted stares — just worry-free, discreet pumping whether you're at work, out with friends, or relaxing at home.\n\nGrab and Go with Confidence\n\nKeep your Mobile Style™ safe and ready to roll with our sleek storage bag. Stylish and practical, it protects your pump and makes carrying it effortless—perfect for busy moms on the move.\n\nOnly 4 Accessories to Wash\n\nCare tip: Do not microwave sterilize. Keep steam sterilizing, drying, or hot-air drying within 100°C / 212°F when possible.\n\n180-Minute Long Battery for All-Day Use\n\nA full charge gives you up to 3 hours of pumping time—enough for 5 to 6 sessions daily. Stay out longer without worrying about discomfort or engorgement.\n\nGREENGUARD Certified\n\nMeets the highest safety and quality standards—safe and gentle for both moms and babies.\n\nTested and Loved by Real Moms\n\nOver 1,000 moms have tested and trusted our products for unbeatable comfort and performance.\n\nDriven by Innovation\n\nOur patented DoubleFit™ design delivers a better, more comfortable breastfeeding and pumping experience.\n\nMobile Style™\n\nPump The Way You Like\n\nGood experience\n\n\"This was an absolute breeze to use. I think it's really worth the price, it's amazing quality, really well made and comes with everything needed to make it a good experience. I found this really effective and it doesn't fall around once in my bra. It's smooth, doesn't feel too heavy, and really is discreet.\"\n\nAmy\n\nFAQs\n\nIs It Good to Use Electric Breast Pumps?\n\nYes! Electric breast pumps are a great choice for breastfeeding moms looking for convenience and efficiency. They can help maintain or increase milk supply, especially for working mothers or those with low supply issues. Choosing the right electric breast pump means finding one that offers strong suction power, quiet operation, and easy-to-use features. A comfortable and effective electric breast pump can make your breastfeeding journey smoother and more successful.\n\nHow Many Minutes Should I Use an Electric Breast Pump?\n\nFor most moms, starting with 15–20 minutes per pumping session is recommended, gradually adjusting based on your milk supply and comfort. Every mom’s needs are different, so listen to your body and pump according to what feels best for you.\n\nFactors like your milk production, your baby’s feeding schedule, and your comfort all play a role. Stop pumping if you feel any discomfort or when your breasts feel empty to avoid over-pumping, which can cause soreness or irritation. Using your electric breast pump correctly helps maintain a healthy milk supply and a comfortable breastfeeding experience.\n\nDo Wearable Pumps Decrease Milk Supply?\n\nA wearable pump does not decrease milk supply, as long as it provides strong and effective suction. Suction strength is key to fully emptying the breast, which helps maintain a healthy milk supply.\n\nWearable pumps like the Momcozy S12 Pro are designed with high suction power to ensure efficient milk removal, so you can pump hands-free without compromising your milk production.\n\nWhich Is Less Painful: Manual or Electric Breast Pump?\n\nPain during pumping varies from mom to mom, but many breastfeeding mothers find electric breast pumps to be less painful because they offer multiple adjustable suction levels and modes, allowing you to customize comfort and reduce nipple pain. However, using too high suction, especially with sensitive nipples or elastic nipples, can still cause discomfort.\n\nSome moms prefer manual breast pumps because they provide more control over suction and pumping speed, which can help minimize pain. Yet, manual pumps may cause hand and wrist fatigue when used for long sessions.\n\nRegardless of whether you choose a manual or electric breast pump, selecting the right breast pump flange size and adjusting the suction level correctly are essential for reducing pain, preventing nipple soreness, and ensuring a comfortable pumping experience.\n\nHow Do I Choose an Electric Breast Pump?\n\nChoosing the right electric breast pump can make all the difference for busy moms. Here are key factors to consider:\n\nPortability:\nIf you pump on the go or at work, choose a lightweight, portable breast pump like the Momcozy M6 that fits your lifestyle.\n\nSuction Power:\nLook for a pump with strong and adjustable suction to effectively express milk and maintain a healthy milk supply.\n\nComfort:\nThe right fit matters — try different pumps and flanges to find one that feels comfortable and prevents nipple pain or discomfort.\n\nFeatures:\nConsider useful features such as double pumping for efficiency, quiet operation for discretion, rechargeable batteries for convenience, and app control for personalized pumping sessions.\n\nPicking the right electric breast pump tailored to your needs helps make breastfeeding easier, more comfortable, and more efficient.\n\nHow should I clean and sterilize M6 accessories?\n\nWash M6 accessories with regular dish soap. If sterilization is needed, boil them for 5 minutes, then air dry, wipe dry, or use low-temperature drying. Do not use microwave sterilization. For steam sterilizing, drying, or hot-air drying, keep the temperature within 100°C / 212°F when possible and do not exceed 110°C / 230°F. M6 a