APP\n\nSize Guide\n\nFAQ\n\nShipping & Delivery\n\nReturn & Exchange\n\nCommunity Discount\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nContact Us\n\nBreastfeeding\n\nMomcozy W1 vs Air 1: Which Wearable Breast Pump Is Right for You?\n\nBy : Momcozy Care Team\n\nLast updated :\nAugust 10, 2026\n\nTable of Contents\n\nPremium Features that Set Them Apart\n\nSleek and Functional Pump Design\n\nComprehensive Pumping Performance Comparison\n\nBattery Life and Charging Convenience\n\nPortability and Noise Level Comparison\n\nUnderstanding the Price Difference\n\nSimple Cleaning and Maintenance\n\nEasy Assembly Process\n\nChoose the Right Model for Your Needs\n\nFind Your Perfect Pumping Partner Today\n\nShow All\n\nChoosing the right breast pump can significantly impact your breastfeeding journey. Momcozy offers two innovative wearable models that cater to different needs: the\nMomcozy Air 1 Ultra-slim Wearable Pump (Air 1)\nand the\nMomcozy Wellness 1 Warm-Massage Wearable Breast Pump (W1)\n. While both deliver efficient pumping performance, they excel in distinct areas. The Air 1 focuses on smart connectivity and ultra-portability, while the W1 introduces revolutionary warm-massage technology for enhanced comfort and milk flow.\n\nPremium Features that Set Them Apart\n\nSmart App Integration on the Momcozy Air 1\n\nThe\n\nAir 1\n\nstands out with its sophisticated smart app control system. By syncing with your smartphone through the Momcozy app, you gain complete control over your pumping experience. Track pumping history, adjust settings remotely, and access professional-recommended patterns including\nMilk Boost™\nfor enhancing production and\nMilk Relief™\nfor easing engorgement discomfort. The\nMyFlow™\nMode allows complete customization, letting you create personalized patterns tailored to your body's unique response.\n\nMomcozy Air 1 Ultra-slim Breast Pump\n\n$314.99 USD\n\n$369.99 USD\n\nUltra-slim\n\nWireless Charging\n\nEffortless Alignment\n\nSmart App Control\n\nMomcozy Wellness 1 Warm-Massage Wearable Breast Pump\n\nFrom\n$329.99 USD\n\nWarm-Massage\n\nMilk Boost Mode\n\nReliable Battery\n\nTransparent Top\n\nTherapeutic Warm-Massage Technology on the Momcozy W1\n\nThe\n\nW1\n\nhas no app control but features integrated warm-massage technology that automates therapeutic techniques directly into your pumping routine.\n\nMomcozy Wellness 1 Warm-Massage Wearable Breast Pump\n\nFrom\n$329.99 USD\n\nWarm-Massage\n\nMilk Boost Mode\n\nReliable Battery\n\nTransparent Top\n\nMomcozy Air 1 Ultra-slim Breast Pump\n\n$314.99 USD\n\n$369.99 USD\n\nUltra-slim\n\nWireless Charging\n\nEffortless Alignment\n\nSmart App Control\n\nWarming Feature: The warming function offers\nthree temperature levels\ndesigned to encourage relaxation and support natural milk flow:\n\n37℃\n: Gentle body-temperature warmth, naturally comforting\n\n39℃\n: Mild spa-like warmth that helps you unwind gradually\n\n41℃\n: Soothing hot-compress heat that encourages flow and promotes relief\n\nTo use the warming feature, simply press the warming button to activate and cycle through the three temperature levels. The petal-shaped warming zone wraps around your breast, creating enveloping warmth across the full contact area. The warming function automatically shuts off after\n15 minutes\nto prevent overstimulation.\n\nMassage Feature:\nThe massage function delivers therapeutic relief through five vibration units with three adjustable intensity levels. To use the massage feature, press the massage button to activate and cycle through the three gentle intensity levels—from light to moderate stimulation. The soft, rhythmic vibrations mimic a baby's natural suckling pattern, helping trigger let-down and support local circulation. Powered by\nexclusive DuoRhythmic™ technology\n, the massage synchronizes with your pumping rhythm—vibrations activate during suction, then pause during relaxation. The massage function automatically stops after 5 minutes to prevent overstimulation.\n\nYou can use the warmth and massage features independently or together for optimal comfort and milk flow.\n\nSleek and Functional Pump Design\n\nBoth the W1 and Air 1 models feature the distinctive tear-drop shape with a flat base design, allowing you to temporarily set them on a table during pumping sessions. Here's a detailed comparison of their design specifications:\n\nDesign Feature\n\nMomcozy Air 1\n\nMomcozy W1\n\nShape\n\nDistinct tear-drop shape\n\nDistinct tear-drop shape\n\nColor Options\n\nOne color\n\nOne color\n\nNumber of Parts\n\n6 parts (motor, flange, diaphragm, valve, milk collector, back cover)\n\n6 parts (motor, flange, diaphragm, valve, milk collector, back cover)\n\nBase Design\n\nFlat base\n\nPlastic foot attachment\n\nIncluded Accessories\n\n1 USB Type-C cable;\n\n1 magnetic charging cable;\n\n2 flange cover\n\n2 USB Type-C cables;\n\n2 flange covers\n\nThe Air 1's ultra-lightweight design at just\n260g\nmakes it incredibly portable, while the W1's slightly heavier build at\n320g\naccommodates the integrated warm-massage technology. Both models provide stability with their base designs, allowing you to set them down safely during pumping sessions.\n\nInnovative Flange Design for Enhanced Comfort\n\nThe Air 1 utilizes soft, flexible flanges for comfortable wear. Meanwhile,\nthe W1 introduces the DoubleFit™ flange system\n, integrating the five-point vibration technology and petal-shaped warming zone directly into the flange design. This creates a more therapeutic pumping experience by combining gentle massage with comforting warmth.\n\nBoth models include a 24mm flange with three flange inserts (17mm, 19mm, and 21mm) to accommodate different breast sizes.\n\nMilk Collection and Stability Features\n\nBoth pumps feature 6-ounce (180ml) milk collectors with stable bases. The Air 1's flat base and W1's plastic foot attachment allow you to safely stand the pump upright before transferring milk to storage containers.\n\nUser-Friendly Controls and Display Options\n\nThe Air 1 keeps controls minimal with button operation and an indicator light system, relying on app connectivity for detailed information and adjustments.\n\nThe W1 features an LED screen displaying real-time pumping data, including mode selection, suction level, session timer, and battery status. This provides at-a-glance information without requiring your phone.\n\nComprehensive Pumping Performance Comparison\n\nPumping power and mode variety are crucial factors that directly affect milk expression efficiency. The Air 1 emphasizes customization with more suction levels and app-controlled patterns, while the W1 focuses on stronger suction power and built-in expert-designed modes. Let's explore how each model performs across different pumping scenarios.\n\nPerformance Feature\n\nMomcozy Air 1\n\nMomcozy W1\n\nMaximum Suction Power\n\n280mmHg\n\n295mmHg\n\nSuction Levels\n\n15\n\n12\n\nStimulation Mode\n\nQuick, short sucking pattern to initiate let-down rapidly\n\nRapid cycling to quickly trigger milk flow\n\nExpression Mode\n\nSlow, deep sucking pattern for efficient milk extraction\n\nDeeper, slower suction for thorough milk expression\n\nMixed Mode\n\nCombines quick and slow patterns for complete emptying\n\nShort and long sucking patterns for gentle, thorough emptying\n\nMilk Boost Mode\n\nApp-exclusive expert pattern to enhance milk production\n\nBuilt-in 30-minute expert cycle simulating natural breastfeeding\n\nAdditional Pumping Patterns\n\nMilk Relief™ (gentle pattern for engorgement via app)\n\nMilk Boost™ (For moms seeking to enhance milk production)\n\nMyFlow™ Mode (fully customizable via app)\n\nFocuses on simplicity with preset modes\n\nKey Advantage\n\nUltimate customization and professional patterns through smart app\n\nOne-touch Milk Boost cycle with warm-massage therapy for maximum comfort and output\n\nThe Air 1 excels in customization with app-controlled professional patterns, while the W1 combines slightly stronger suction with therapeutic warm-massage technology for enhanced comfort and milk release.\n\nBattery Life and Charging Convenience\n\nThe\nAir 1\noffers flexible charging options with two convenient methods. First, you can use the included charging case to power up your pump—simply align the pump's charging port with the case slot, and the indicator will flash green during charging, turning solid white when fully charged. The case takes about 3 hours to fully charge alone, or about 5 hours when charging both the case and two pumps simultaneously.\n\nSecond, you can charge the pump directly using the magnetic charging cable with a 5V/2A adapter (adapter sold separately). The Air 1's internal rechargeable battery takes approximately 150 minutes to fully charge and provides about 6 sessions of 30-minute pumping. When the battery indicator turns red, you have roughly 30 minutes of use remaining. For detailed visual instructions on charging the Air 1, refer to\nthis video guide\n.\n\nThe\nW1\nfeatures a 2200mAh battery charged via USB cable. A full charge provides up to10 sessions of standard pumping or 6 sessions when using warm-massage features, ensuring reliable performance throughout your day.\n\nPortability and Noise Level Comparison\n\nThe\nAir 1\nweighs 260g and includes a compact charging-carrying case, making it exceptionally portable for working moms. It operates at ≤45dB, ensuring discreet use anywhere.\n\nThe\nW1\nweighs 320g without a carrying case. Due to its warm-massage motors, it operates at ≤50dB, which is still relatively quiet but slightly louder than the Air 1.\n\nUnderstanding the Price Difference\n\nThe Momcozy\nW1\nretails at $329.99, while the\nAir 1\nis priced at $369.99. The $40 difference reflects the Air 1's smart technology and charging case versus the W1's therapeutic warm-massage features.\n\nSimple Cleaning and Maintenance\n\nIt is important to keep the breast pump hygienic for the sake of the baby’s health and hygiene. Both Air 1 and W1 breast pumps have similar processes for\ncleaning\nafter each use.\n\nBefore Every Use:\nInspect and assemble a clean pump. Clean the motor surface with disinfectant wipes, and ensure all parts that contact breast milk and skin are thoroughly cleaned and disinfected before use.\n\nAfter Every Use:\n\nDisassemble all pump parts that contacted milk or breast. For the Air 1, detach the flange from the pump, grip the protrusions to remove the milk collector from the main unit, remove the diaphragm, disassemble the milk collector, and separate the valve.\n\nRinse all parts thoroughly with clean water immediately after pumping\n\nWash with mild dish soap and warm water\n\nAir dry completely on a clean surface before reassembly\n\nStore milk safely in breast milk storage bags or food-grade containers with tight-fitting lids, labeled with date and time\n\nEasy Assembly Process\n\nBoth models have a\nsimple assembly procedure\n. Once you have cleaned and dried all components thoroughly, you can follow these easy steps:\n\nAttach the valve to the milk collector and ensure it is securely installed\n\nAssemble the milk collector, making sure the front and back covers are tightly secured\n\nClose the stopper on the milk collector\n\nAttach the diaphragm to the milk collector. First, secure the silicone and plastic parts of the diaphragm, then install it inside the back cover of the milk collector, ensuring it fits securely.\n\nMake sure the main unit and the flange are tightly assembled to prevent air leakage.\n\nConnect the milk collector assembly to the main unit, ensuring the flange or insert is the correct size and properly fitted\n\nClick\nhere\nfor more details about the assembly process.\n\nSafety Reminders:\n\nAlways wash your hands with soap before handling pump components and breasts to avoid contamination.\n\nMake sure each part is cool if it was disinfected by boiling.\n\nExamine components before every use for evidence of damage, such as cracks, chips, tears, or discoloration; stop using if da