ut a bulky outline. The charging case covers a run of sessions away from a plug. If a shared room means noise matters more than profile, choose M9.\n\nIs the Momcozy Air 1 easy to use for first-time mums?\n\nYes. The transparent top lets you see the nipple is centred before you start — usually the hardest step on a wearable. There are five parts to wash, buttons on the cup, and the app only if you want it. You can express without opening your phone.\n\nHow do I use the Air 1 ultra-slim breast pump?\n\nWash and assemble the five milk-contact parts. Keep the motor dry.\n\nPlace the cup in your bra. Use the transparent top to centre the nipple in the tunnel.\n\nTurn on. Choose Stimulation, Expression or Mixed on the cup or in the app, then pick a suction level that feels comfortable — not the highest.\n\nWhen the 180 ml collector is full, the app can alert you. Switch off, take the motor off, then pour.\n\nHow do I centre the flange on the Air 1?\n\nLook through the transparent top and check the nipple sits in the middle of the tunnel, not pulled to one side. Measure nipple diameter, not bra cup. Air 1 ships with a 24 mm flange and 17/19/21 mm inserts. Pain, a white ring, or too much areola being pulled in means resize before you turn suction up.\n\nCan I track expressing sessions and milk volume?\n\nYes. The Momcozy app can switch modes, show milk volume as you go, alert you when the collector is full, and keep a session history. The pump still runs from the buttons on the cup if you would rather not use the phone.\n\nHow long does the Air 1 charging case last?\n\nThe case holds enough power for up to 15 sessions of about 30 minutes. Seat each pump so the contacts line up; the case tops them up and stores them for a work day or a few days out. Charge the case from a plug at home, then take it with you.\n\nHow do I clean and sterilise the Air 1 ultra-slim breast pump?\n\nTake the motor off first and wipe it dry only — never soak it. Rinse the five milk-contact parts (c