\n\nAPP\n\nSize Guide\n\nFAQ\n\nShipping & Delivery\n\nReturn & Exchange\n\nCommunity Discount\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nContact Us\n\nBreastfeeding\n\nMomcozy M5 Smart vs M6: Which Wearable Breast Pump Is Right for You?\n\nBy : Momcozy Care Team\n\nLast updated :\nAugust 10, 2026\n\nTable of Contents\n\n1. Product Design\n\n2. App Control\n\n3. Pumping Power, Modes, and Performance\n\n4. Charging Battery\n\n5. Portability\n\n6. Price\n\n7. Cleaning and Maintenance\n\n8. Which Breast Pump Is Right for You?\n\nM5 Smart vs M6: The Final Verdict\n\nShow All\n\nThe Momcozy M5 Smart vs M6 is one of the most common comparisons new moms face.\nThe M5 Smart is the upgraded version of the M5, Amazon's #1 best-selling breast pump in 2024, and it now adds app connectivity to an already trusted design. The M6 brings a more powerful second-generation motor with stronger suction and longer battery life\n. This guide breaks down every key difference so you can choose with confidence.\n\nFeature\n\nM5 Smart\n\nM6\n\nPrice\n\n$199.99\n\n$229.99\n\nDESIGN\n\nShape\n\nSemi-circular\n\nTear-drop\n\nColors\n\n2 variants\n\n2 variants\n\nFlat base (table-safe)\n\nNo\n\nYes\n\nFlange type\n\n100% soft silicone, 105°\n\nDoubleFit™ hard+soft silicone, 105°\n\nFlange sizes\n\n17/19/21/24mm (27mm optional)\n\n17/19/21/24mm (27mm optional)\n\nCAPACITY & DISPLAY\n\nMilk collection cup\n\n5.4 oz (160ml)\n\n6 oz (180ml)\n\n5-inch HD screen\n\nMode + suction level; battery at startup only\n\nMode + suction + real-time battery + timer; backlight dims after 45s\n\nPERFORMANCE\n\nMotor\n\n1st Generation\n\n2nd Generation\n\nMax suction (expression)\n\n-285 mmHg\n\n-295 mmHg\n\nModes / Suction levels\n\n3 modes, 9 levels\n\n3 modes, 9 levels\n\nApp control\n\nYes (iOS 13 / Android 8.0+)\n\nNo\n\nSession tracking\n\nAuto-log: volume, time, trends\n\nBuilt-in timer only\n\nBATTERY & PORTABILITY\n\nBattery life\n\n4–5 sessions (~150 min)\n\n5–6 sessions (~180 min)\n\nCharge time\n\n~120 min\n\n~150 min\n\nWeight\n\n8.1 oz (230g)\n\n10.1 oz (287g)\n\nNoise level\n\n50 dB or less\n\n50 dB or less\n\nCarrying case\n\nIncluded\n\nIncluded (slightly larger)\n\n1. Product Design\n\nOverall Design\n\nBoth the M5 Smart and M6 are compact, all-in-one wearable pumps that require no tubing. Each model comes in 2 color variants and includes 5 main parts, one USB-C charging cable, and one flange cover.\n\nThe shape is where the two pumps differ. The M5 Smart features a semi-circular profile that sits flush and discreetly in a nursing bra. It measures 5.0 x 4.6 x 2.9 inches (128mm x 117mm x 74mm). The M6 has a distinct tear-drop shape that more closely mimics the natural contour of the breast, giving it an even more discreet look under clothing. It measures 5.1 x 4.5 x 2.9 inches (130mm x 114mm x 73mm).\n\nOne practical advantage of the M6 is its\nflat base\n. After removing the pump from your bra, you can place it upright on a table while you transfer your milk, without any risk of tipping.\n\nFlange Design\n\nThe\nM5 Smart\nfeatures a 100% soft silicone flange with a 105° slope. This angle is designed to mimic the natural curve of a baby's latch, which reduces pressure on milk ducts and supports a more comfortable pumping experience. The soft lip stretches over the edge of the collection cup to form a seal, which is a common wearable pump design. It does require careful assembly each time to maintain good suction.\n\nThe\nM6\nfeatures the DoubleFit™ flange, which combines hard and soft silicone and also includes the 105° slope. The hard component clicks securely into the collection cup, creating a reliable seal with a lower chance of leaks or suction loss. The soft cushion wraps around the breast for a snug, comfortable fit throughout each session.\n\nM6 Milk Cooler Bundle: M6 Hands-free Breast Pump and Portable Baby Bottle Cooler\n\n$318.99 USD\n\nM5 Smart Wearable Breast Pump – Upgraded with App Control\n\nFrom\n$119.99 USD\n\nComfort Fit\n\nSteady Output\n\nHands-Free Freedom\n\nEasy App Control\n\nBoth models come standard with a 24mm flange and three inserts in 17mm, 19mm, and 21mm sizes to suit different nipple diameters. For moms who need a larger size, 27mm flanges are available separately for both pumps.\n\nMilk Collector\n\nThe M5 Smart milk collector holds\n5.4 oz (160ml)\n, which is enough for most full pumping sessions. The M6 collection cup holds 6 oz (180ml), giving moms with a stronger letdown or longer sessions a bit more room before needing to empty.\n\nThere is also an important handling difference. The M5 Smart collection cup cannot stand on its own once detached, so you need to keep it flat or transfer the milk right away to avoid spills. The M6 pump has a flat base that allows it to stand upright on a surface independently, even when full. This frees up both hands so you can organize your storage bags and containers without rushing.\n\nLED Screen\n\nThe M5 Smart has a basic LED display showing the current mode and suction level. Battery life is only visible when you first power the pump on.\n\nThe M6 has a larger, clearer LED screen that shows the mode, suction level, real-time battery life, and a built-in\nsession timer\nall at once. For nighttime pumping, the M6 screen also has a backlight that makes it easy to check your settings without turning on a light. The backlight automatically dims after 45 seconds of no interaction, keeping things discreet during night feeds.\n\n2. App Control\n\nApp connectivity is one of the most significant differences between these two pumps.\n\nThe M5 Smart connects to the Momcozy app via Bluetooth and is compatible with iOS 13 and Android 8.0 or higher. Through the app, you can adjust pumping modes and suction levels directly from your phone without reaching under your clothing. The app also unlocks a\nPersonalized mode\nbeyond the three standard modes.\n\nSession tracking\nis automatic. The app logs the time, duration, and volume of every session and displays your trends in daily, weekly, and monthly graphs. You can set custom pumping reminders, track which breast was pumped, and export your data to share with a\nlactation consultant\nwhen needed.\n\nThe M6 has no app connectivity. All adjustments are made directly on the pump using the physical buttons. For moms who prefer simplicity and do not want to manage a separate app, the M6's clear LED screen puts all the essential information right in front of you.\n\n3. Pumping Power, Modes, and Performance\n\nThe M5 Smart uses Momcozy's 1st generation motor. The M6 upgrades to a 2nd generation motor, which delivers stronger suction and a more consistent pumping rhythm across all modes.\n\nBoth pumps offer three modes with nine suction levels each:\n\nStimulation Mode\n: begins with a quick, short sucking pattern to trigger milk letdown.\n\nExpression Mode\n: switches to a slow, deep sucking pattern for efficient milk extraction.\n\nMixed Mode\n: starts with a quick, short sucking pattern and then transitions to a slow, long sucking pattern for thorough drainage.\n\nThe table below compares vacuum ranges and cycle speeds across all three modes:\n\nSpec\n\nM5 Smart\n\nM6\n\nMotor\n\n1st Generation\n\n2nd Generation\n\nStimulation vacuum\n\n-75 to -145 (±30) mmHg\n\n-75 to -145 (+5) mmHg\n\nExpression vacuum\n\n-120 to -285 (±30) mmHg\n\n-120 to -295 mmHg\n\nMixed vacuum\n\n-75 to -285 (±30) mmHg\n\n-75 to -295 mmHg\n\nStimulation speed\n\n50-120 (±2) cycles/min\n\n70-88 (±2) cycles/min\n\nExpression speed\n\n23-57 (±2) cycles/min\n\n27-60 cycles/min\n\nMixed speed\n\n6-16 (±2) cycles/min\n\n56-82 cycles/min\n\nThe M6 reaches a higher maximum suction in expression and mixed modes, up to -295 mmHg compared to -285 mmHg for the M5 Smart. The M6's cycle speeds are also faster and more consistent, particularly in stimulation and mixed modes, which means quicker letdowns and more efficient sessions overall.\n\n4. Charging Battery\n\nBoth pumps use USB-C charging and cannot be used while charging. The charging process is the same for both models.\n\nThe M5 Smart delivers approximately 4 to 5 pumping sessions, or about 150 minutes of total use based on 30-minute sessions, per full charge. It takes around 120 minutes to charge from empty.\n\nThe M6 delivers approximately 5 to 6 pumping sessions, or about 180 minutes of total use, per full charge. It takes around 150 minutes to charge fully. The extra 30 minutes of battery life makes a real difference on busy days, and for moms who pump frequently or need the pump to last through a full workday, the M6 holds a clear advantage.\n\n5. Portability\n\nBoth pumps are designed for life on the go. They both operate at\n50 dB or less\n, roughly the same noise level as a quiet library, so you can pump discreetly at the office, in a cafe, or next to a sleeping baby.\n\nThe M5 Smart is the lighter option at 8.1 oz (230g) with all accessories attached. The M6 weighs 10.1 oz (287g). The difference is noticeable but not a burden, especially if your bag is already packed with baby essentials.\n\nBoth pumps come with a hard-shell carrying case that keeps everything organized and protected during travel. The M6's case is slightly larger to accommodate its bigger design. Both cases fit the pump, flange inserts, charging cable, and storage bags comfortably.\n\n6. Price\n\nThe M5 Smart retails at $199.99 USD. The M6 is priced at $229.99 USD, a $30 difference.\n\nFor that extra investment, you get a more powerful 2nd generation motor, longer battery life, a pump that stands on its own, a more informative LED screen with a built-in timer, and a larger collection cup. If budget is your top priority, the M5 Smart delivers strong, reliable performance at a lower price. If you want premium features and a smoother day-to-day pumping experience, the M6 makes that $30 feel well spent.\n\n7. Cleaning and Maintenance\n\nThe\nbottle cleaning and sterilization\nprocess is the\nsame for both the M5 Smart and M6\n, making it easy to build into your daily routine.\n\nBefore every use,\ninspect your pump kit and wipe the motor unit with disinfectant wipes. Always wash your hands thoroughly with soap and water before touching any pump parts.\n\nAfter every use,\ndisassemble the four milk-contact parts: the flange, diaphragm, valve, and milk collector. Rinse them under clean running water, then wash in a dedicated clean basin (not directly in the sink) with warm soapy water at 104-140°F (40-60°C) for 3 to 5 minutes. Use a brush reserved for infant feeding items. Rinse thoroughly again and air dry completely on a clean towel. Do not rub items dry with a cloth, as this can transfer germs.\n\nFor daily disinfection,\nplace the cleaned milk-contact parts in a pot of fresh drinking-quality water, bring to a boil, and boil gently for 3 minutes. Make sure no parts touch the sides of the pot to avoid damage. Remove with clean tongs and air dry fully. Do not use a microwave, UV sterilizer, or dishwasher. Temperatures above 230°F (110°C) will damage the silicone and plastic parts and shorten their service life.\n\nFor the motor unit,\nwipe the exterior with 70% isopropyl alcohol wipes and use a soft cloth to remove any visible residue. Allow it to air dry at room temperature for about 10 minutes. The motor must never be submerged in water or put in a dishwasher.\n\nAs a general maintenance tip,\ninspect your valves and silicone diaphragms regularly and replace them every 1 to 3 months depending on how often you pump. Worn parts can reduce suction and affect overall performance.\n\n8. Which Breast Pump Is Right for You?\n\nChoose the M5 Smart if:\n\nYou want to control and monitor your pumping sessions directly from your phone.\n\nTracking session data such as volume, duration, and trends matters to you, especially if you work with a lactation consultant.\n\nYou prefer a lighter pump at 8.1 oz (230g) and want to save $30.\n\nYou want the most feature-rich upgrade of the best-selling M5, with app control included at the same price point.\n\nChoose the M6 if:\n\nYou want a stronger 2nd generation motor for faster, more efficient pumping sessions.\n\nLonger battery life is a priority. With 5 to 6 sessions per charge, the M6 is built to last through a full workday.\n\nThe flat-base design appeals to you. Being able to set the pump down independently after removing it is a genuine daily convenience.\n\nYou prefer a no-app experience with a clear, information-rich LED screen that includes a built-in timer and real-time battery display.\n\nIn short:\nthe M5 Smart is the right choice for tech-savvy moms who want smart tracking and app control. The M6 is the right choice for moms who want stronger performance, longer battery life, and added everyday convenience.\n\nM5 Smart vs M6: The\n\nFinal\n\nVerdict\n\nBoth the Momcozy M5 Smart and M6 are well-built, hands-free pumps designed to fit real life\n. The M5 Smart gives you app-powered tracking and control at a budget-friendly price point, building on the legacy of the best-selling M5. The M6 gives you stronger suction, a longer-lasting battery, and thoughtful design upgrades. Whichever you choose, you are investing in a pump built to support your breastfeeding journey every step of the way.\n\nDisclaimer\n\nThe information provided in this article is for general informational purposes only and does not constitute medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Always seek the advice of your physician or other qualified health provider regarding any medical condition. Momcozy is not responsible for any consequences arising from the use of this content.\n\nRelated articles\n\n22\n\nSep\n\nBreastfeeding\n\nUsing a Nursing Pillow With a Reflux Baby: The Safe Answer on Elevation Angles\n\n0\ncomment\n\ndetails\nRead more\n\n22\n\nSep\n\nBreastfeeding\n\nFirm vs Plush Nursing Pillow: Positioning Support in the First 6 Weeks\n\n0\ncomment\n\ndetails\nRead more\n\n22\n\nSep\n\nBreastfeeding\n\nHow to Pump During Chemotherapy or Medication Windows: A Safe, Drug-Specifi