de breast pump?\n\nMomcozy M9 is a wearable, personal breast pump with\nhospital-grade suction power\n. It is helpful to know the distinction between a \"hospital-grade\" pump and \"hospital-grade suction.\"\n\nA \"hospital-grade\" breast pump is really a multi-user, rental pump designed for use in a hospital or clinic setting. They are made in a closed system so the milk won't get into the motor or tubing, so they can be shared with many mothers safely. They are most commonly for moms who need to establish their milk supply or moms with a baby in the NICU.\n\nOn the other hand, \"hospital-grade suction power\" refers to the suction power and cycle rate of the pump. This is used to refer to a pump that can produce sufficient suction to well initiate and maintain a milk supply by mimicking a powerful suckling baby.\n\nBrief and to the point, the Momcozy M9 delivers powerful performance you need in a convenient, hands-free configuration that's perfect for personal, in-your-home-on-the-go applications. Unless you have a medical need for a multi-user pump, a personal pump with hospital-grade suction like the M9 should be ample power for your daily pumping needs.\n\nWhat is the suction level of the Momcozy M9?\n\nThe Momcozy M9 offers a powerful\nmaximum suction strength of -300mmHg\n, which is designed to be highly effective for milk expression. To give you full control and comfort, the pump provides 3 distinct modes:\n\nStimulation Mode to gently stimulate let-down.\n\nExpression Mode for efficient milk output.\n\nMixed Mode which alternates between the two for a more natural feel.\n\nYou can further fine-tune the suction intensity across a total of 15 adjustable levels within these modes, allowing you to find the perfect setting for your comfort and milk flow.\n\nWhich is better, Momcozy M5, M6 or M9?\n\nThere is no single \"best\" pump among the Momcozy M5, M6, and M9;\nthe best choice depends on your personal needs and pumping style. The\nkey differences lie in their design, motor power, and advanced\nfeatures.\n\nHere is a comparison of their main features to help you decide:\n\nFeature\n\nMomcozy M5\n\nMomcozy M6\n\nMomcozy M9\n\nDesign\n\nSemi-circular shape, manual button control, lightweight\n\nTear-drop shape, flat base, larger LED screen, button control\n\nTear-drop shape, flat base, larger LED screen, App & button\ncontrol, modern look\n\nMotor\n\n1st Gen (Basic)\n\n2nd Gen (Stronger than M5)\n\n3rd Gen (Most powerful)\n\nSuction Levels\n\n9 levels\n\n9 levels\n\n15 levels\n\nWeight\n\n230g\n\n287g\n\n302g\n\nModes\n\n3 modes\n\n3 modes\n\n3 modes + 2 professional patterns (Milk Boost™ & Milk Relief™;\nthese two patterns are app-controlled only)\n\nMilk Collector\n\n5.4 oz (160ml), cannot stand on its own\n\n6 oz (180ml), flat base stands independently to prevent spills\n\n5 oz (150ml), flat base stands independently, with lids for\ntemporary storage\n\nFlange\n\n100% soft silicone\n\nDoubleFit (hard & soft silicone), secure seal\n\nDoubleFit (hard & soft silicone), snug fit\n\nKey Advantage\n\nBudget-friendly, simple, and ideal for occasional or first-time\npumpers.\n\nLeak-proof design, larger capacity, and reliable performance.\n\nApp control, most powerful motor, and advanced features for frequent\npumpers.\n\nSummary:\n\nChoose the\nM5\n\nif you are an occasional pumper or prefer a simple, gadget-free\nexperience with a more budget-friendly pump.\n\nChoose the\nM6\n\nif you need a reliable pump with a larger capacity and a secure,\nspill-proof design, making it great for multitasking.\n\nChoose the M9\nif you are a frequent or exclusive\npumper who wants the most powerful motor, maximum customization with app\ncontrol, and advanced features to track and optimize your\nsessions.\n\nFor a more in-depth feature comparison, you can read our detailed\nblog posts:\nMomcozy\nM5 vs.M6\ncomparison and\nMomcozy\nM5 vs. M9 comparison\n.\n\nCan I get Momcozy M9 through insurance?\n\nYes\n, you can get a Momcozy M9 breast pump