who need a reliable, efficient, and discreet solution. As a hands-free breast pump, the M9 features powerful suction and efficient milk extraction—all in a lightweight, wearable design.\n\nWith app-controlled settings, you can easily adjust suction levels, modes, and track milk output right from your phone—no need to interrupt your routine. The portable and stackable milk collectors make it easy to pump on the go and store milk without the mess.\n\nWhether you're juggling work, travel, or just daily life, the Momcozy M9 gives you the freedom to pump wherever and whenever you need, with comfort, confidence, and total control.\n\nDo Wearable Pumps Decrease Milk Supply?\n\nA wearable pump does not decrease milk supply, as long as it provides strong and effective suction. Suction strength is key to fully emptying the breast, which helps maintain a healthy milk supply.\n\nWearable pumps like the Momcozy S12 Pro are designed with high suction power to ensure efficient milk removal, so you can pump hands-free without compromising your milk production.\n\nCan I Exclusively Pump with a Hands-Free Pump?\n\nYes, you can exclusively pump with a hands-free breast pump. In fact, many moms find hands-free pumping to be a convenient and effective way to build and maintain milk supply, especially when nursing isn’t an option.\n\nThe key is using a high-performance pump that fully empties the breasts. A smart, wearable option like the Momcozy M9, with powerful suction up to -300 mmHg and a comfortable DoubleFit™ flange, is designed to support exclusive pumping, without compromising comfort or milk output.\n\nFor the best results, it’s a good idea to consult with a lactation professional to create a pumping schedule that matches your goals.\n\nWhat Is a Good Hands-Free Pump?\n\nA good hands-free breast pump should offer strong suction, a comfortable fit, and quiet operation — all while giving moms the freedom to pump while multitasking. Look for a pump with adjustable suction levels, 