\n\nAPP\n\nSize Guide\n\nFAQ\n\nShipping & Delivery\n\nReturn & Exchange\n\nCommunity Discount\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nContact Us\n\nBreastfeeding\n\nMomcozy Air 1 vs M5 Smart: Which Wearable Breast Pump Is Right for You?\n\nBy : Momcozy Care Team\n\nLast updated :\nAugust 10, 2026\n\nTable of Contents\n\nQuick Decision Guide: Which Pump Is Right for You?\n\n1. Smart App Control\n\n2. Pump Design: Slim Profile vs. Familiar Shape\n\n3. Pumping Modes and Suction Performance\n\n4. Battery Life and Charging\n\n5. Portability and Noise\n\n6. Cleaning and Maintenance\n\n7. Assembly\n\n8. Price\n\n9. Which Pump Should You Choose?\n\nFull Specifications at a Glance\n\nFinal Thoughts\n\nShow All\n\nWhen you compare the Momcozy Air 1 vs M5 Smart, the choice comes down to how much you pump, where you pump, and how much you want to spend. Both pumps connect to the Momcozy app and fit inside your bra. But the Air 1 targets moms who need a\nslim profile\nand a\ncharging case\nfor all-day freedom, while the M5 Smart delivers solid app-connected performance at a much friendlier price.\n\nQuick Decision Guide: Which Pump Is Right for You?\n\nNot sure where to start? This table zeroes in on what actually matters when choosing between these two pumps.\n\nIf you care most about...\n\nM5 Smart\n\nAir 1\n\nBudget\n\n$199.99 (save $170)\n\n$369.99\n\nOn-the-go charging\n\nStandard carry case only\n\nCharging case doubles as power bank for up to 15 sessions\n\nExtra pumping modes\n\n3 standard modes only\n\nMilk Boost™, Momcozy Warming Lactation Massager Pro™ + MyFlow™ personalized pattern\n\nDiscretion under clothing\n\nSemi-circular, 2.9 in (74 mm) thick\n\nTear-drop, just 2.4 in (61 mm) thin, 20% slimmer\n\nNoise level\n\n48 dB or below\n\n45 dB or below\n\nSuction control\n\n9 levels, up to 285 mmHg\n\n15 levels, up to 280 mmHg\n\nMilk collector\ncapacity\n\n5.4 oz (160 ml), no flat base\n\n6 oz (180 ml),\nflat base\n, stays upright\n\nBottom line\n\nBest value for reliable app-connected pumping\n\nBest for travel, busy work schedules, and advanced features\n\n1. Smart App Control\n\nBoth the Air 1 and the M5 Smart connect to the Momcozy app via Bluetooth, so you can adjust pumping settings and track your sessions from your phone without reaching under your clothing.\n\nThe\n\nM5 Smart\n\napp lets you start and stop pumping, switch between modes, adjust suction levels (1 to 9), and log your milk output by session, day, week, or month. You can control both pumps at the same time or adjust each side individually. You can also operate the M5 Smart using the physical buttons on the pump directly without the app.\n\nThe\nAir 1\ngoes further. It includes everything the M5 Smart app offers, plus three exclusive pumping patterns available only through the app.\nMilk Boost\n™ uses scientifically optimized rhythms to help enhance milk production.\nMilk Relief\n™ gently eases engorgement while expressing milk.\nMyFlow\n™ lets you fully customize your own stimulation, expression, or mixed mode pattern. You can save your favorite patterns and build routines that work best for your body.\n\nM5 Smart Wearable Breast Pump – Upgraded with App Control\n\nFrom\n$119.99 USD\n\nComfort Fit\n\nSteady Output\n\nHands-Free Freedom\n\nEasy App Control\n\nMomcozy Air 1 Ultra-slim Breast Pump\n\n$314.99 USD\n\n$369.99 USD\n\nUltra-slim\n\nWireless Charging\n\nEffortless Alignment\n\nSmart App Control\n\nThe Air 1 app also features\nAutomatic mode switching\n, which automatically transitions from\nStimulation mode (let-down trigger)\nto\nS12 Pro Expression mode\nso you do not have to adjust settings mid-session. Real-time milk tracking shows a visual fill indicator at 60 ml, 120 ml, and 180 ml, and sends a push notification when the collector is nearly full. The M5 Smart does not support Milk Boost™,\nMilk Relief\n™, or\nMyFlow\n™.\n\n2. Pump Design: Slim Profile vs. Familiar Shape\n\nOverall Shape, Size, and Components\n\nThe\nM5 Smart\nhas a semi-circular shape measuring 5.04 in x 4.61 in x 2.91 in (128 mm x 117 mm x 74 mm). It comes in two colors: Cozy Red and Quill Grey. The pump has 5 main parts (motor, flange, diaphragm, valve, milk collector), and includes a USB-C charging cable and a flange cover.\n\nThe\nAir 1\nhas a teardrop shape measuring 4.92 in x 4.33 in x 2.40 in (125 mm x 110 mm x 61 mm). It comes in one color and has 6 main parts (motor, flange, diaphragm, valve, milk collector, milk collector back cover), and includes both a USB Type-C cable and a magnetic charging cable, plus a flange cover. At just 2.4 inches (6.1 cm) thin, it is over 20% slimmer than other conventional pumps. For a closer look at the Air 1 design,\nwatch this overview video\n.\n\nThe Air 1 also has a flat base, so you can set it down on a desk or table without worrying about it tipping over and spilling your milk. The M5 Smart has a rounded base, so you need to pour the milk into a\nclean storage container\nright after removing the pump.\n\nFlange Design and Sizing\n\nThe\nM5 Smart\nfeatures Momcozy's patented DoubleFit™ flange with a horizontal pumping angle that mimics the natural curvature of a baby's mouth during nursing. This design improves pumping efficiency by 28.2% and reduces leakage by 10%.\n\nThe\nAir 1\nuses soft, flexible 50A silicone flanges that gently conform to your breast shape for added comfort during longer sessions.\n\nBoth pumps include a 24 mm flange and three flange inserts for S9 Pro/S12 Pro (17 mm, 19 mm, and 21 mm). If you need a 27 mm breast pump flange for larger nipple sizes, the M5 Smart offers it as a separate purchase. This option is not currently available for the Air 1.\n\nMilk Collector\n\nThe M5 Smart milk collector holds 5.4 oz (160 ml) and has a rounded base. The Air 1 milk collector holds 6 oz (180 ml) and has a flat, stable base that sits on a surface without tipping, a helpful detail for busy pumping sessions.\n\nDisplay\n\nThe M5 Smart has an\nLED screen\nshowing your current mode, suction level (1 to 9), and battery status at startup. The Air 1 has no LED screen and uses a simple indicator light instead: solid white for full battery, solid red for low battery (one cycle left), flashing green while charging, and solid green when fully charged. All detailed monitoring on the Air 1 happens through the app.\n\n3. Pumping Modes and Suction Performance\n\nBoth pumps offer three standard modes. Stimulation Mode uses a quick, short sucking pattern to trigger your let-down reflex. Expression Mode switches to a slow, deep suction to draw out milk efficiently. Mixed Mode begins with a fast pattern and then transitions to a slow, deep pattern.\n\nThe Air 1 offers\n15 suction levels\nwhile the M5 Smart offers 9. Both pumps include a 30-minute auto shut-off and a memory function that remembers your last-used settings. Here is a detailed look at the vacuum and cycle speed ranges:\n\nMode\n\nAir 1 Vacuum Range\n\nM5 Smart Vacuum Range\n\nCycle Speed (cycles/min)\n\nStimulation\n\n-67.5 to -172.5 mmHg\n\n-75 to -145 mmHg\n\nAir 1: 54-90 / M5 Smart: 50-120\n\nExpression\n\n-105 to -280 mmHg\n\n-120 to -285 mmHg\n\nAir 1: 25-60 / M5 Smart: 23-57\n\nMixed\n\n-67.5 to -280 mmHg\n\n-75 to -285 mmHg\n\nAir 1: 46-84 / M5 Smart: 6-16\n\nThe Air 1's 15 suction levels give you finer control over intensity, which is especially helpful if you are sensitive to pressure changes or working through supply challenges. Note that the exclusive app modes (Milk Boost™, Milk Relief™, MyFlow™) are available on the Air 1 only, not the M5 Smart.\n\n4. Battery Life and Charging\n\nThe\nM5 Smart\ncharges via USB Type-C in about 120 minutes and provides up to 180 minutes of use, approximately 6 pumping sessions at 30 minutes each.\n\nThe\nAir 1\noffers two charging methods: a USB Type-C cable and a magnetic charging cable. The pump battery charges in about 140 minutes and provides 180 minutes of use. For a walkthrough of how to use the Air 1 charging case,\nwatch this video\n.\n\nThe standout advantage of the Air 1 is its\nwireless charging case\n. The case holds up to 1,800 mAh and powers up to 15 pumping sessions, giving you approximately 5 days of use without needing a wall outlet. Simply place the pump into the case and it charges wirelessly. The M5 Smart comes with a hard-shell carrying case for protection, but it does not charge your pump.\n\n5. Portability and Noise\n\nThe Air 1 weighs 9.2 oz (260 g) and operates at\nunder 45 dB\n, making it one of the quietest wearable pumps available and quiet enough to use during video conferences or in shared office spaces. The M5 Smart weighs 8.2 oz (232 g) and operates at\nunder 48 dB\n, which is still very discreet for most everyday environments.\n\nThe Air 1's transparent top panel lets you visually confirm nipple alignment without undressing, which saves time and reduces guesswork when you are out and about.\n\n6. Cleaning and Maintenance\n\nKeeping your pump clean is essential because germs grow quickly in breast milk residue. Both pumps follow the same core cleaning steps.\n\nAfter every use, disassemble all parts that contacted your breast or milk. Rinse them immediately with cold water, then wash with warm soapy water in a clean basin used only for baby feeding items. Rinse again with clean water and air dry on a clean dish towel or paper towel. Never pat parts dry with a cloth towel as this can transfer germs.\n\nFor\ndaily sanitization of breast pumps\n, place the disassembled milk-contact parts in a pot of water, bring to a boil, and boil for 5 to 10 minutes. Make sure parts do not touch the sides of the pot to avoid warping. Remove with clean tongs and air dry completely before reassembling.\n\nNever put the motor unit, charging cable, or adapter in water or a dishwasher. Wipe the motor with 70% isopropyl alcohol wipes only. The Air 1 has one extra part to clean (the milk collector back cover). Replace silicone valves and diaphragms every 1 to 3 months depending on your pumping frequency.\n\n7. Assembly\n\nBoth pumps go together in under 30 seconds. Always wash your hands first, and let boiled parts cool completely before touching them.\n\nAssembling the Air 1\n\nPush the valve gently into the milk collector until no gaps remain.\n\nAssemble the milk collector by securing the parts together.\n\nAttach the diaphragm to the milk collector and secure the back cover to form a tight seal.\n\nHolding the two edge protrusions, attach the collector to the main unit.\n\nInstall the flange onto the pump.\n\nAssembling the M5 Smart\n\nAttach the diaphragm to the milk collector, pressing gently around the edge until it seals.\n\nPush the valve into the flange until no gaps remain.\n\nAlign the flange with the milk collector so the patterns overlap, then press down firmly with your thumbs.\n\nAttach the pump motor to the assembled milk collector.\n\n8. Price\n\nThe M5 Smart double pump is priced at\n$199.99\n. The Air 1 double pump is priced at\n$369.99\n. That is a $170 difference. The Air 1's higher cost reflects its ultra-slim design, quieter operation, larger milk collector, charging case with power bank capability, additional professional app modes, and auto mode switching. Both pumps include a carrying case and a one-year warranty.\n\n9. Which Pump Should You Choose?\n\nChoose the Momcozy M5 Smart if:\n\nYou want reliable app-connected pumping at a budget-friendly price.\n\nYou prefer a pump you can operate with physical buttons without needing your phone.\n\nYou want a 27 mm flange option available for larger nipple sizes.\n\nYou primarily pump at home or in comfortable environments where whisper-quiet operation is not a must.\n\nYou want excellent everyday value without paying for features you may not use.\n\nChoose the Momcozy Air 1 if:\n\nYou pump frequently away from home and need a wireless charging case that supports up to 15 sessions without a wall outlet.\n\nYou need to pump in very quiet environments such as shared offices or public spaces.\n\nYou want access to Milk Boost