 pump for most UK mums: app control, a 230 g cup, and suction up to −285 mmHg. Start here if you want an in-bra pump with a phone app and no extra hardware.\n\nDiscreet at work\n\nAir 1\n\nAir 1 is the slimmest all-in-one wearable at 61 mm, with a charging case for longer days out. Choose it when a lower in-bra profile matters under work clothes, especially if you’re\npumping at work\n.\n\nApp control, quieter motor\n\nM9\n\nM9 is the quieter all-in-one wearable (≤42 dB), with app control, 15 suction levels and up to −300 mmHg. Pick it if you want finer control and a lower motor note.\n\nDaily power, no app\n\nM6\n\nM6 gives up to −300 mmHg without an app. Choose it if you want a simple daily wearable and you’d rather skip Bluetooth.\n\nStarting on a budget\n\nS12 Pro Quick\n\nS12 Pro Quick is the entry all-in-one wearable if you want in-bra pumping at a lower price, with a 210 ml cup and a quicker clean.\n\nCompare\n\nAll Momcozy pumps on this page\n\nUse Type if you’re unsure. All-in-one wearable means tube-free: the motor sits in the cup. Separate unit, in-bra cups means collection cups in the bra and the motor outside.\n\nModel\n\nType\n\nSuction\n\nBattery\n\nWeight\n\nNoise\n\nApp\n\nPrice\n\nAir 1\n\nAll-in-one wearable\n\nUp to −280 mmHg\n\nUp to 15 sessions with case\n\n260 g\n\n≤45 dB\n\nYes\n\n£369.99\n\nWellness 1\n\nAll-in-one wearable\n\nUp to −295 mmHg\n\nAbout 10 sessions; about 6 with warmth\n\n320 g\n\n<50 dB\n\nYes\n\n£299.99\n\nM5 Smart\n\nAll-in-one wearable\n\nUp to −285 mmHg\n\nAbout 6 sessions\n\n230 g\n\n<48 dB\n\nYes\n\nFrom £99.99\n\nM9\n\nAll-in-one wearable\n\nUp to −300 mmHg\n\n4–5 sessions\n\n302 g\n\n≤42 dB\n\nYes\n\nFrom £159.99\n\nM6\n\nAll-in-one wearable\n\nUp to −300 mmHg\n\n5–6 sessions\n\n287 g\n\n≤50 dB\n\nNo\n\nFrom £129.99\n\nS12 Pro Quick\n\nAll-in-one wearable\n\nUp to −292 mmHg\n\nAbout 8 sessions\n\n240 g\n\n≤46 dB\n\nNo\n\nFrom £79.99\n\nV1 Pro\n\nSeparate unit, in-bra cups\n\nUp to −300 mmHg\n\nAbout 9 sessions\n\n240 