n\nAPP\n\nSize Guide\n\nFAQ\n\nShipping & Delivery\n\nReturn & Exchange\n\nCommunity Discount\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nContact Us\n\nBreastfeeding\n\n8 Best Pumps to Increase Milk Supply: Picks for New Moms\n\nBy : Momcozy\n\nLast updated :\nAugust 10, 2026\n\nTable of Contents\n\nWhy Do You Have Low Milk Supply?\n\nHow To Increase and Maximize Milk Supply with Pumping\n\nHow to Choose the Best Breast Pump for Low Milk Supply?\n\nTop 8 Breast Pumps to Increase Milk Supply\n\nFAQs about Best Breast Pumps for Low Supply\n\nConclusion\n\nShow All\n\nLow milk supply happens when a mother doesn’t produce enough breast milk to meet her baby’s needs. Some signs are the baby not gaining enough weight, having fewer wet diapers, or being hungry after feeding. Many factors can affect milk supply, and it’s important to know the signs and ways to boost it, like utilizing a\nbreast pump to increase milk supply\n. In this article, you will learn the best of the best pumps to increase your milk supply.\n\nWhy Do You Have Low Milk Supply?\n\nLow milk supply can happen for many reasons. It is often related to how breastfeeding starts and how it is managed. According to the\nUNICEF Organization\n, some reasons why you have a low milk supply are delays in breastfeeding, not enough skin-to-skin contact, or issues during delivery that can affect how quickly milk comes in.\n\nFeeding issues, like poor latch, short feeds, or sticking to a strict schedule instead of feeding when the baby is hungry, can also reduce milk supply. Skipping night feeds and not feeding often enough are other common causes. Producing a low milk supply can also be caused by taking certain\nbirth control pills\nor other medicines, drinking alcohol, smoking, or insufficient sleep.\n\nUnderstanding this and taking action is the most appropriate thing to do. Pumping or expressing your milk frequently using the best breast pump for low supply between nursing sessions and consistently when you’re away from your baby can help build your milk supply.\n\nHow To Increase and Maximize Milk Supply with Pumping\n\nThe key to increasing milk supply is always emptying your breasts. It lets your body know that there is a demand, and thus, your body will produce more to meet that. The best way to do it is through breastfeeding, but that is not always an option. You may need to empty your breast while your baby is still full or asleep. This is where breast pumps come in. They allow you to express milk in these situations and store the supply for later use.\n\nWith that said, you should have a consistent pumping schedule. Ideally, you want to pump 8 - 12 times within 24 hours. This helps ensure that your breasts are never full and milk production does not stop.\n\nHow to Choose the Best Breast Pump for Low Milk Supply?\n\nThe correct pump helps maximize milk expression by providing efficiency, customizable settings, and comfort. When selecting the best pump for a low milk supply, several critical factors must be considered, including function and fit.\n\nHigh suction strength\n- The best pump for low milk supply should have a high suction strength for efficient milk expression. Higher suction strength helps to stimulate milk production and ensures that you can effectively empty your breasts, which can lead to increased milk supply over time. Look for the breast pump for low milk supply with adjustable suction levels to customize the intensity according to your comfort and needs.\n\nElectric pumps\n-\nElectric pumps\nare often more effective than the best manual breast pump for low milk supply for frequent and consistent use. They offer steady and dependable suctions without the need for physical exertion. The best electric breast pump for low milk supply offers various settings to mimic a baby’s natural feeding pattern.\n\nDouble\n- The best pump to increase milk supply should have a\ndouble-pumping\n, enabling simultaneous milk expression on both breasts. Double pumping can also enhance let-down reflexes and improve milk flow.\n\nComfortable\n- A\nwell-fitting flange\nis the best pump to increase milk supply. Flanges that are the correct size and shape for your breasts can prevent discomfort and ensure a proper seal, which helps to maximize milk flow. Since comfort is also key during the feedings that follow your pumping sessions, using a\nnursing pillow\ncan provide the necessary ergonomic support to bottle-feed your baby without straining your arms or back.\n\nPortable\n- Choose\nthe best wearable breast pump\nfor a low milk supply that is easy to carry and use wherever you go. To increase your milk supply, you must pump often; a compact and lightweight pump can simplify your daily routine.\n\nQuiet\n- A breast pump for a low milk supply that runs quietly can help you feel more relaxed during pumping sessions. Less noise can make the experience more comfortable and help with low milk flow.\n\nEasy to clean\n- Choose the best breast pump for increasing supply that is simple to take apart and clean. Easy-to-clean parts make it faster to keep everything hygienic and reduce time spent on maintenance.\n\nPremium Feature (Warm-Massage Breast Pump)\n- If you have trouble with milk letdown or flowing slowly, look for special features. A\nwarm-massage breast pump\n, like the\nMomcozy W1\n, uses gentle warmth and rhythmic massage to relax you. This helps your body release the hormone (oxytocin) that makes milk come out. Using both together is great for getting the most milk and building up your supply, making it a top choice if you have low milk supply.\n\nTop 8 Breast Pumps to Increase Milk Supply\n\nIf you’re dealing with a low milk supply, choosing the best pump to increase milk supply can be a game changer. An effective pump and the best breast pump for increasing supply help you express more milk and encourage increased production by mimicking a baby’s natural feeding patterns. Here are the 8 best breast pumps to increase milk supply:\n\n1. Momcozy\n\nMomcozy W