rs.\n\nSummary:\n\nChoose the\nM5\n\nif you are an occasional pumper or prefer a simple, gadget-free\nexperience with a more budget-friendly pump.\n\nChoose the\nM6\n\nif you need a reliable pump with a larger capacity and a secure,\nspill-proof design, making it great for multitasking.\n\nChoose the M9\nif you are a frequent or exclusive\npumper who wants the most powerful motor, maximum customization with app\ncontrol, and advanced features to track and optimize your\nsessions.\n\nFor a more in-depth feature comparison, you can read our detailed\nblog posts:\nMomcozy\nM5 vs.M6\ncomparison and\nMomcozy\nM5 vs. M9 comparison\n.\n\nCan I get Momcozy M9 through insurance?\n\nYes\n, you can get a Momcozy M9 breast pump through your insurance by working with one of our Durable Medical Equipment (DME) partners.\n\nA DME partner is a professional firm that helps you get medical devices like breast pumps under your insurance plan. They approach your insurance company directly to provide the verification, authorization, and claims process on your behalf. You will require a prescription from a health care provider, e.g., a doctor or midwife, to begin with.\n\nThe most significant reasons for obtaining your pump from a DME partner are:\n\nCost Savings\n: The pump is generally paid for by the insurance at little or no cost to you.\n\nHassle-Free Process\n: Your DME partner takes care of all paperwork and communication with your insurance company.\n\nExpert Guidance\n: They will arrange for all appropriate documentation to be submitted to meet insurance requirements.\n\nApart from the M9, our other top-selling breast pump models, the M5 and M6, can also be obtained through insurance.\n\nOur insurance partners and process information can be viewed on the\n\nMomcozy Insurance Partners in US\n\npage.\n\nWhich is better, Spectra or Momcozy M9?\n\nBoth Spectra and Momcozy are trusted breast pump brands, but they are designed for different user needs, so the best choice depends on your lifestyle.\n\nSpectra is best known for its traditional pumps with a large main unit and tubing that connects them. These pumps are most often used in a stationary setting, focusing on powerful, hospital-grade suction for optimal efficiency.\n\nIn comparison, the Momcozy M9 is a wearable, hands-free breast pump. Due to its all-in-one, foldable format, you can wear it in your bra while moving about, multitasking, or pumping anywhere without being tethered with tubes or plugged in. Therefore, if discretion and mobility are your top priorities, a wearable pump like the M9 is your best bet.\n\nWhat Makes Momcozy M9 a Good, Smart, and Hands-Free Breast Pump?\n\nThe Momcozy M9 smart breast pump is designed for today’s busy moms who need a reliable, efficient, and discreet solution. As a hands-free breast pump, the M9 features powerful suction and efficient milk extraction – all in a lightweight, wearable design.\n\nWith app-controlled settings, you can easily adjust suction levels, modes, and track milk output right from your phone, with no need to interrupt your routine. The portable and stackable milk collectors make it easy to pump on the go and store milk without the mess.\n\nWhether you're juggling work, travel, or just daily life, the Momcozy M9 gives you the freedom to pump wherever and whenever you need, with comfort, confidence, and total control.\n\nDo Wearable Pumps Decrease Milk Supply?\n\nA wearable pump does not decrease milk supply, as long as it provides strong and effective suction. Suction strength is key to fully emptying the breast, which helps maintain a healthy milk supply.\n\nWearable pumps like the Momcozy S12 Pro are designed with high suction power to ensure efficient milk removal, so you can pump hands-free without compromising your milk production.\n\nCan I Exclusively Pump with a Hands-Free Pump?\n\nYes, you can exclusively pump with a hands-free breast pump. In fact, many moms find hands-free pumping to be a convenient and effective way to