{"anchor": "#l.1-3", "char_count": 4000, "heading_path": null, "kb_type": "wording", "meta": {"anchor_precision": "segment_only", "content_quality_flag": "recrawl_headless_rendered", "content_quality_note": "2026-09-29 统一口径无头渲染正文"}, "order_in_parent": 3, "pair_ref": null, "parent_unit_id": null, "resource_id": "url__https____ca.momcozy.com_products_momcozy-mobile-style-hands-free-breast-pump", "rule_eligible": true, "rule_eligible_run": "20260924-1730", "rule_eligible_source": "not_material_collection", "source_sha256": "2bb73617ff5aa097952d05f596d68abae9d35adbf357f36555adce7b190264ca", "splitter_version": "l2-0.3", "splitter_version_backfilled_at": null, "text": "by’s feeding schedule, and your comfort all play a role. Stop pumping if you feel any discomfort or when your breasts feel empty to avoid over-pumping, which can cause soreness or irritation. Using your electric breast pump correctly helps maintain a healthy milk supply and a comfortable breastfeeding experience.\nDo Wearable Pumps Decrease Milk Supply?\nA wearable pump does not decrease milk supply, as long as it provides strong and effective suction. Suction strength is key to fully emptying the breast, which helps maintain a healthy milk supply.\nWearable pumps like the Momcozy S12 Pro are designed with high suction power to ensure efficient milk removal, so you can pump hands-free without compromising your milk production.\nWhich Is Less Painful: Manual or Electric Breast Pump?\nPain during pumping varies from mom to mom, but many breastfeeding mothers find electric breast pumps to be less painful because they offer multiple adjustable suction levels and modes, allowing you to customize comfort and reduce nipple pain. However, using too high suction, especially with sensitive nipples or elastic nipples, can still cause discomfort.\nSome moms prefer manual breast pumps because they provide more control over suction and pumping speed, which can help minimize pain. Yet, manual pumps may cause hand and wrist fatigue when used for long sessions.\nRegardless of whether you choose a manual or electric breast pump, selecting the right breast pump flange size and adjusting the suction level correctly are essential for reducing pain, preventing nipple soreness, and ensuring a comfortable pumping experience.\nHow Do I Choose an Electric Breast Pump?\nChoosing the right electric breast pump can make all the difference for busy moms. Here are key factors to consider:\nPortability: If you pump on the go or at work, choose a lightweight, portable breast pump like the Momcozy M6 that fits your lifestyle.\nSuction Power: Look for a pump with strong and adjustable suction to effectively express milk and maintain a healthy milk supply.\nComfort: The right fit matters — try different pumps and flanges to find one that feels comfortable and prevents nipple pain or discomfort.\nFeatures: Consider useful features such as double pumping for efficiency, quiet operation for discretion, rechargeable batteries for convenience, and app control for personalized pumping sessions.\nPicking the right electric breast pump tailored to your needs helps make breastfeeding easier, more comfortable, and more efficient.\nHow should I clean and sterilize M6 accessories?\nWash M6 accessories with regular dish soap. If sterilization is needed, boil them for 5 minutes, then air dry, wipe dry, or use low-temperature drying. Do not use microwave sterilization. For steam sterilizing, drying, or hot-air drying, keep the temperature within 100°C / 212°F when possible and do not exceed 110°C / 230°F. M6 accessories can also be cleaned in a Momcozy bottle washer, but please do not use Storage mode. Avoid alcohol-based cleaners, as they may affect the soft silicone on the flange.\nWhy does the suction feel weaker after cleaning or sterilizing?\nSuction may feel weaker if the milk collector or flange is slightly deformed after excessive heat exposure, which can affect the airtight seal. Please check whether the accessories are fully dry, properly installed, and free from warping, gaps, or damage. To help maintain strong suction, avoid microwave sterilization and keep steam sterilizing, drying, or hot-air drying within the recommended temperature range.\n98% would recommend this product\nReviews 626 (tab expanded) Questions 1 (tab collapsed)\nWrite a Review (Opens in a new window)\nSort Most Recent Oldest Most Helpful Photos & Videos Highest Rating Lowest Rating Least Helpful\nI've used it twice. The first time i had some leakage but i readjusted and it works perfectly! It has strong suction. I use the Medela Pump in pro as my main pump and I feel like I get pretty similar output. I got this pump a", "unit_id": "859084a7a64305cbc1a4", "unit_type": "clause"}
