ny pumps you own but having the right type available when each pumping session calls for it ( Cleveland Clinic breast pump guide ).\nDo I need different flange sizes for wearable vs. traditional pumps?\nYes -- flange (breast shield) sizing can differ between pump types. Traditional pumps often offer more flange size options and third-party inserts, making it easier to dial in the perfect fit. Wearable pumps may have fewer sizing choices, so double-check the available sizes before purchasing. An ill-fitting flange can reduce milk output and cause discomfort -- especially problematic when you are pumping for two. Medela's sizing guidance recommends re-measuring your nipple s", "unit_id": "939447e8cb2375f15828", "unit_type": "clause"}
