bag without needing to pour or clean up right away.\nAdditionally, the M9 double pump comes with four milk collection containers, while the single pump includes two. This design gives moms more than just backups—it’s about easy storage. After pumping, you can simply screw on a lid and store the full container directly in the fridge. When it’s time for the next session, just swap in the extra containers and keep going without delay.\nLED Screen: Clear Info at a Glance\nBoth the Momcozy M6 and M9 come equipped with a backlit LED screen that displays all the essentials during your pumping session:\nCurrent mode (Stimulation, Expression, or Mixed)\nThe backlight makes night pumping easier, letting you check your settings without switching on room lights—a must-have for sleepy midnight sessions. For added discretion, the screen's light automatically turns off after 45 seconds of inactivity, helping you stay low-profile whether you're in bed or in a shared space.\nExclusive to the M9 is a toggle button that allows you to select which breast you're pumping—left or right—making it easier to track your sessions and maintain balance if you alternate sides. This thoughtful small addition adds an extra layer of control, and is especially useful when paired with the app's tracking feature.\nIn terms of screen layout and readability, the two models are identical, offering a simple-to-use, familiar interface with no learning curve.\nFor pumping performance, both the Momcozy M6 and M9 are designed to support milk expression efficiently and comfortably—but the M9's upgraded motor and app-based control system offer more flexibility for moms with sensitive needs or changing supply.\nM6 is powered by Momcozy's 2nd Generation motor\nM9 uses the 3rd Generation motor, which delivers more precise suction and quieter performance\nThis hardware difference gives the M9 an edge, particularly when fine-tuning is needed.\nBoth models feature three standard pumping modes to simulate a natural feeding rhythm:\nStimulation Mode : Short, fast cycles to trigger milk let-down\nExpression Mode : Deeper, slower suction to draw out milk\nMixed Mode : Starts with stimulation, then shifts into expression automatically\nThese core modes are designed to meet the needs of most moms across different stages of their pumping routine.\nM9 Exclusive App-Based Patterns\nAvailable only via the Momcozy app, the M9 offers three advanced pumping programs tailored for specific challenges:\nMilk Boost™ : Supports milk supply rebuilding—ideal for moms returning to work or rebuilding stash\nMilk Relief™ : Offers gentle suction to ease engorgement or clogged ducts\nMyFlow™ : Fully customizable mod", "unit_id": "834dda44d99ffc4fed5c", "unit_type": "clause"}
