venient USB-C charging.\nUp to 180 minutes (5–6 sessions)\nUp to 150 minutes (4–5 sessions)\nM6: Lightweight with Lasting Power\nDespite having a smaller battery capacity (1350mAh), the M6 delivers up to 180 minutes of pumping per full charge, enough for 5 to 6 sessions. It's ideal for moms who pump multiple times daily and need the freedom to go longer between charges. Whether you're working a long shift or out running errands, the M6's runtime helps reduce anxiety about mid-day power drops.\nM9: Higher Battery Capacity, More Power-Demanding Features\nThe M9 packs a larger 1800mAh battery, but because of its app connectivity and more powerful 3rd-gen motor, its runtime is slightly shorter—about 150 minutes per charge, translating to 4 to 5 full pumping sessions. For many moms, that's still more than enough to cover a workday, especially when paired with the added functionality and control the app offers.\nBoth models use a USB-C port with a dust plug, making charging simple and travel-friendly. Just plug in at night and wake up ready for the day—no proprietary adapters or wall cradles required.\nWhether you're heading to work, running errands, or simply trying to pump discreetly during a stroll, portability matters. Both Momcozy M6 and M9 are designed for hands-free freedom—but there are subtle differences that can shape your daily convenience.\nWith a total weight of just 287g (around the weight of a 300ml drink), the M6 is slightly lighter than the M9. It comes with a stylish storage case that offers excellent protection, though the case itself is slightly bulkier, which some users mention takes up more space in compact diaper bags or carry-ons. That said, the shape and form are still travel-friendly, making it easy to take along for longer outings.\nM9: Compact and Ultra-Discreet\nWeighing in at 302g, the M9 is marginally heavier, but its slimmer overall profile and more compact storage case give it an edge in tight-packing scenarios. Designed to fit seamlessly 