hm.Momcozy S12 Pro Quick is designed to make every pumping...\nV1 Pro Hospital-Strength Wearable Breast Pump\nV2 Pro Hospital-Strength Wearable Breast Pump - Ultra-light & Potent\nS9 Pro Wearable Breast Pump Upgraded - Long Battery Life\nOne charge for one daySupport 9 pumping sessions20% smaller motor to carry lighterCome in 4 sizes (17/19/21/24mm)Seal-up connection for bigger suctionUpgraded the LED screen to view the battery life\nM5 Smart Double Wearable Breast Pump + 120 Breastmilk Storage Bags Bundle\nGentle, Breast-Friendly Pumping Baby mouth-like suction rhythm, skin-friendly silicone, and 30-minute auto stop help make daily pumping feel gentler and more comfortable. Patented DoubleFit™ Flange for a Better Fit The...\nM5 Smart Bra Bundle: Double M5 Smart Breast Pump and Nursing Bra(YN21)\nExperience everyday comfort with our top-of-the-line wireless nursing and M5 Smart Breast Pump!\nM6 Bra Bundle: M6 Hands-free Breast Pump and Nursing Bra-YN21\nFeeding Bundle: M5 Smart Wearable Breast Pump and 120 Breastmilk Storage Bags and Nursing Bra YN21\nM5 Smart Bra Bundle: Double M5 Smart Breast Pump and Jelly Strip Bra(YN46)\nM9 Bra Bundle: M9 Breast Pump and YN46 Nursing Bra\nV1 Pro Bra Bundle: V1 Pro Breast Pump and US. Cotton Nursing Bra\nS9 Pro Bra Bundle: Double S9 Pro and Jelly Strip Bra\nS9 Pro Bag Bundle: Double S9 Pro Pumps and Breastmilk Storage Bags\nFeeding Bundle:S12 Pro Quick and 4-in-1 Hands Free Pumping Bra and 120 Breastmilk Storage Bags\nM5 Smart Wearable Breast Pump & KleanPal Pro Baby Bottle Washer and Sterilizer Bundle\nPump & Clean Bundle: M6 Hands-free Breast Pump and KleanPal Pro Baby Bottle Washer and Sterilizer\nPump & Clean Bundle: M9 Hands-free Breast Pump and KleanPal Pro Baby Bottle Washer and Sterilizer\nPump & Clean Bundle: M9 Breast Pump and Bottle Washer and Washing Block\nWhich electric breast pump is right for you?\nThere isn’t one best electric breast pump. It depends what you need it for: everyday pumping, a slimmer cup for longer days out, warmth and massage, or a hospital-strength motor off your chest.\nM5 Smart is the everyday electric breast pump for most UK mums: an app, a 230 g cup, and suction up to −285 mmHg. Start here if you want everything in your bra and a phone app.\nAir 1 is the slimmest all-in-one electric at 61 mm, with a charging case for longer days out. Choose it if you want a slimmer cup under clothes.\nWellness 1 warms the cup and adds massage with the suction rhythm, with three warmth levels at 37°C, 39°C and 41°C. App control, so you can adjust warmth and massage from your phone.\nHospital-strength, motor off the chest\nV1 Pro is the hospital-strength electric if you want the cups in your b", "unit_id": "d03cd61b5644d30db94a", "unit_type": "clause"}
{"anchor": "#l.1-2", "char_count": 4000, "heading_path": null, "kb_type": "wording", "meta": {"anchor_precision": "segment_only", "content_quality_flag": "recrawl_headless_rendered", "content_quality_note": "2026-09-29 统一口径无头渲染正文"}, "order_in_parent": 2, "pair_ref": null, "parent_unit_id": null, "resource_id": "url__https____uk.momcozy.com_collections_electric-breast-pump", "rule_eligible": true, "rule_eligible_run": "20260924-1730", "rule_eligible_source": "not_material_collection", "source_sha256": "4d317e7b6da5e7a06810dd905b44a780382c5781ce5aa00e43d5cafab773c431", "splitter_version": "l2-0.3", "splitter_version_backfilled_at": null, "text": "ra and the motor off your chest: 15 levels, up to −300 mmHg, for longer sessions at home. V2 Pro is the same type with a 127 g motor if you want a lighter unit.\nAll-in-one wearable means the motor sits in the cup, with no tubes. Separate unit, in-bra cups means hospital-strength electric with the motor outside. Then check suction, battery and price.\nAbout 10 sessions; about 6 with warmth\nPortable and wireless electric breast pumps\nA portable breast pump runs on battery, so you’re not tied to a wall socket. All of these electric pumps do that.\nA wireless breast pump is the same idea: no mains lead in the wall while you express.\nWant everything in the bra and no tubes? Choose an all-in-one. Want the motor off your chest? Choose V1 Pro or V2 Pro.\nIf you want tube-free in-bra pumping as well as cordless power, see the Wearable collection .\nElectric vs manual breast pumps\nChoose an electric breast pump if you pump most days, you’re going back to work, or you want both sides done in one session. A motor does the squeezing for you, and most have a let-down mode then an expression mode, so it takes less time. You pay more, and you charge it.\nChoose a manual pump if you only express now and then, or want a quiet spare with no charging. It’s slower if you need a lot of milk every day.\nMost electric kits are doubles, so you can express both sides in one session and cut the time. If feeding isn’t going well, speak to your midwife or health visitor.\nBags, bras and a bottle washer\nOnce you switch the motor off, you still need to store the milk, keep the cups in place, and wash the parts.\nUse breast milk storage bags to label and freeze milk flat. Follow NHS guidance on how long milk keeps. A storage jug is useful at home if you prefer to pour milk together before you bag it.\nA pumping bra holds the cups in place so your hands are free while you pump. An ordinary stretchy bra can work; a pumping bra is more likely to stay put.\nA bottle washer washes and sterilises pump parts in one go, so you’re not facing a sink of parts after every session. It is faster than cleaning breast pump parts by hand. Add a washing block if you want the detergent measured for you.\nWhat to check on an electric breast pump\nIf you want the whole pump in your bra with no tubes, start with M5 Smart. Pick Air 1 if you need a slimmer cup, Wellness 1 if you want in-cup warmth and massage, or M6 if you’d rather skip an app. If you’d rather keep the motor off your chest, choose V1 Pro, or V2 Pro for a lighter unit.\nSize the cup to your nipple, not your bra size. Most kits include a 24 mm flange and 17, 19 and 21 mm inserts. If pumping hurts, you see a white ring, or too much breast is pulled in, try another size before you turn the suction up.\nThese pumps charge with USB-C, like a phone. Top up from a wall plug, a laptop or a power bank, then pump on battery at home, at work or out. If you’ll be away from a charger for several sessions, pick one that lasts longer on a charge. Warmth uses more battery.\nIf you pump both sides most days, a double kit is quicker. Only buy a single if you usually express one side, or you want a spare.\nWhen you know which type you want, check suction, battery and breast pump price .\nWhat is an electric breast pump?\nAn electric breast pump uses a motor to express milk, so you’re not squeezing a handle. You can get ones that sit fully in your bra with no tubes, or stronger pumps where the cups go in your bra and the motor stays outside.\nWhich electric breast pump is best?\nThere isn’t one best pump for every mum. Most people start with M5 Smart for everyday use. Choose Air 1 if you want a slimmer cup and a charging case. Choose Wellness 1 if you want in-cup warmth and massage. Choose V1 Pro if you want a stronger motor off your chest.\nWhat’s the difference between the two types of electric pump?\nThe difference is where the motor sits. One type has the motor in the cup: no tubes, the whole pump goes in your bra. That’s M5 Smart, Air 1, Wellness 1, M6", "unit_id": "61e9e8caa566be5b703e", "unit_type": "clause"}
{"anchor": "#l.1-3", "char_count": 2778, "heading_path": null, "kb_type": "wording", "meta": {"anchor_precision": "segment_only", "content_quality_flag": "recrawl_headless_rendered", "content_quality_note": "2026-09-29 统一口径无头渲染正文"}, "order_in_parent": 3, "pair_ref": null, "parent_unit_id": null, "resource_id": "url__https____uk.momcozy.com_collections_electric-breast-pump", "rule_eligible": true, "rule_eligible_run": "20260924-1730", "rule_eligible_source": "not_material_collection", "source_sha256": "4d317e7b6da5e7a06810dd905b44a780382c5781ce5aa00e43d5cafab773c431", "splitter_version": "l2-0.3", "splitter_version_backfilled_at": null, "text": ", M9, S12 Pro Quick and S9 Pro. The other type still puts the cups in your bra, but the motor sits outside on a short tube. That’s V1 Pro and V2 Pro — hospital-strength, with the motor off your chest. Choose the no-tube type if you want to move around with nothing hanging off you. Choose V1 Pro or V2 Pro if you’d rather keep a stronger motor off your chest.\nAre V1 Pro and V2 Pro wearable pumps?\nYes. In the UK, wearable usually means the cups sit in your bra so you can move around. V1 Pro and V2 Pro do that — the motor just sits outside, with tubing. They are not the tube-free, all-in-one kind.\nIs a portable or wireless breast pump the same as a wearable?\nNo. Portable or wireless just means it runs on battery, so you’re not plugged into the wall while you pump. Wearable means the cups sit in your bra. Most of these pumps are both: cordless, with the cups in the bra.\nShould I get an electric or a manual pump?\nGo electric if you pump most days, you’re going back to work, or you want both sides done in one go. A manual pump is fine if you only express now and then, and you want something quiet with no charging.\nCan I pump both sides at once?\nYes. Most electric kits do both sides together, which is the usual choice if you express from both breasts. A few are also sold as a single — only pick that if you usually pump one side, or you want a spare.\nDo I need a pumping bra or storage bags?\nYou can pump without them, but most mums who express every day end up wanting both. A pumping bra holds the cups so your hands are free. Bags let you label and freeze milk for later.\nHow should I store expressed milk?\nFollow the NHS. They currently say fridge for up to 8 days at 4°C or lower, and freezer at −18°C or lower for up to 6 months. Some NHS pages also allow up to 6 hours at room temperature. Check the NHS expressing page for the latest.\nCan an electric pump help with engorgement?\nIt can take the pressure off if you feel uncomfortably full. If you think you have mastitis, feeding hurts, or baby is not getting milk, talk to your midwife or health visitor.\nGlobal No.1 Wearable Breast Pump Brand*\n*According to Grand View Research's Wearable Breast Pump Market Analysis and Segment Forecasts to 2030 (2024), Momcozy ranked No.1 globally in the Wearable Breast Pump category based on total market share in 2024. Rankings are based on the methodology and market definition used in the report.\nBe among the first to receive updates on our latest products, product innovations, and exclusive offers.\nSign up now for sale alerts & special offers.\nSuite 302, 4 Station Square, Cambridge,\n(Calls cost Xp plus your phone company's access charge)\nFirst Year Baby Cost Calculator\nAll Rights Reserved © 2026 Momcozy.\nChoosing a selection results in a full page refresh.", "unit_id": "6b501ac67a7e6bc07f62", "unit_type": "clause"}
