the hormone involved in milk let-down.\nHow does the heating feature on the Momcozy Wellness 1 work, and is it a safe heated breast pump?\nThe Wellness 1 uses a wraparound warmth design that works like a built-in warm compress on the flange area. You can choose 3 temperature levels (37°C / 39°C / 41°C) . Warmth automatically stops after 15 minutes, and massage after 5 minutes.\nThis warming breast pump is designed to give wide, gentle heat that helps the breast relax during your session, with temperatures limited to these set levels.\nWhat is the difference between the Momcozy Wellness 1 and the Air 1?\nBoth are wearable pumps with app control, but they are built for different needs. The Wellness 1 adds wraparound warmth and rhythmic vibration massage, so heat, massage and suction can work together. The Air 1 does not have heat or massage; it is the slimmer option and includes a charging case, which the Wellness 1 does not. Choose the Wellness 1 if you want a warm-massage pumping session; choose the Air 1 if a slim profile and charging case matter more.\nHow does the Momcozy Wellness 1 compare to a standard pump?\nA standard pump typically uses suction alone, and many are not designed to be worn in the bra. The Wellness 1 is a wearable breast pump and a heated breast pump in one: it adds r hythmic massage and wraparound warmth to suction. That is why it is also described as a warming, hands-free breast pump — heat and massage are built in, rather than added with a separate compress or massager.\nHas the Momcozy Wellness 1 been tested for safety and does it have certifications?\nYes, absolutely. We tested the motor and all parts of the Momcozy Wellness 1 very carefully. Experts checked them to make sure they are safe, strong and built to last. Rest assured that this breast pump complies with all relevant safety standards and certifications, making it a reliable companion for your entire feeding journey. If you have pain, inflammation or a breast infection, speak to y